any?","correct":"The Company","wrong":["Planet Scrap Co.","Lethal Robotics","Gordian Shipping Co."]},{"id":"d48c0a169194","q":"What is the nickname of the US state of California?","correct":"Golden State","wrong":["Sunshine State","Bay State","Treasure State"]},{"id":"2769b3b85587","q":"Which of the following carbonated soft drinks were introduced first?","correct":"Dr. Pepper","wrong":["Coca-Cola","Sprite","Mountain Dew"]},{"id":"f466803882b2","q":"What is real haggis made of?","correct":"Sheep's Heart, Liver and Lungs","wrong":["Sheep's Heart, Kidneys and Lungs","Sheep's Liver, Kidneys and Eyes","Whole Sheep"]},{"id":"c53b341c7e79","q":"What was Mountain Dew's original slogan?","correct":"Yahoo! Mountain Dew... It'll tickle your innards!","wrong":["Give Me A Dew","Do The Dew","Get' that barefoot feelin' drinkin' Mountain Dew"]},{"id":"b630474c0b57","q":"Frank Lloyd Wright was the architect behind what famous building?","correct":"The Guggenheim","wrong":["Villa Savoye","Sydney Opera House","The Space Needle"]},{"id":"b71110b655b6","q":"What does the F stand for in the FBI?","correct":"Federal","wrong":["Foreign","Formal","First"]},{"id":"ef358cfc34cc","q":"What is the most-visited website out of these options?","correct":"Google","wrong":["YouTube","Facebook","Wikipedia"]},{"id":"b7009d4dc1a2","q":"What is the French word for \"fish\"?","correct":"poisson","wrong":["fiche","escargot","mer"]},{"id":"9280a98ef78d","q":"What does the Latin phrase \"Veni, vidi, vici\" translate into English?","correct":"I came, I saw, I conquered","wrong":["See no evil, hear no evil, speak no evil","Life, liberty, and happiness","Past, present, and future"]},{"id":"7b10c8f2f412","q":"Which country has the most Trappist breweries?","correct":"Belgium","wrong":["Netherlands","France","USA"]},{"id":"36c06af8e700","q":"What is a \"dakimakura\"?","correct":"A body pillow","wrong":["A Chinese meal, essentially composed of fish","A yoga posture","A word used to describe two people who truly 