, what is Moneko / MISS Moneko's critical percentage rate?","correct":"15%","wrong":["20%","10%","25%"]},{"id":"ad190b14ce3d","q":"The tale of Robin Hood originates from which country?","correct":"England","wrong":["France","Portugal","Scotland"]},{"id":"ef9a35ff9eef","q":"Computer manufacturer Compaq was acquired for $25 billion dollars in 2002 by which company?","correct":"Hewlett-Packard","wrong":["Toshiba","Asus","Dell"]},{"id":"28e3c969d7f2","q":"Which language is NOT Indo-European?","correct":"Hungarian","wrong":["Russian","Greek","Latvian"]},{"id":"19544716d4c7","q":"In Half-Life, what is the name of the alien that attaches to heads?","correct":"Headcrab","wrong":["Bullsquid","Vortigaunt","Facehugger"]},{"id":"613e377e676e","q":"What is the Spanish word for \"donkey\"?","correct":"Burro","wrong":["Caballo","Toro","Perro"]},{"id":"db0e546b8721","q":"What element has the chemical symbol Kr?","correct":"Krypton","wrong":["Kerosine","Kineticium","Curium"]},{"id":"f0a94961af7f","q":"All Souls and Merton are constituent colleges of what university?","correct":"Oxford","wrong":["Cambridge","Manchester","Leeds"]},{"id":"a53495e77b90","q":"Before the 19th Century, the \"Living Room\" was originally called the...","correct":"Parlor","wrong":["Open Room","Sitting Room","Loft"]},{"id":"0bca0b231fe6","q":"This field is sometimes known as “The Dismal Science.”","correct":"Economics","wrong":["Philosophy","Politics","Physics"]},{"id":"642d9304d35a","q":"The Canadian $1 coin is colloquially known as a what?","correct":"Loonie","wrong":["Boolie","Foolie","Moodie"]},{"id":"cb0b443482f1","q":"What is the name of the poker hand containing three of a kind and a pair?","correct":"Full House","wrong":["Flush","Straight","High card"]},{"id":"99c55ba50e4c","q":"Rolex is a company that specializes in what type of product?","correct":"Watches","wrong":["Cars","Computers","Sports equipment"]},{"id":"1ddd2f9f85c2","q":"Gouda cheese is from which European country?","correct":"The Netherla