e;land"]},{"id":"d082261ab777","q":"In which country was the Michelin tire company founded in 1889?","correct":"France","wrong":["United Kingdom","Italy","Germany"]},{"id":"7779a2454a5f","q":"Who was the 1st President of Mexico?","correct":"Guadalupe Victoria","wrong":["Benito Ju&aacute;rez","Miguel Hidalgo Y Costilla","Vicente Guerrero"]},{"id":"cd05af50506f","q":"What does a funambulist walk on?","correct":"A Tight Rope","wrong":["Broken Glass","Balls","The Moon"]},{"id":"0c04c9c71094","q":"What is the romanized Russian word for \"winter\"?","correct":"Zima","wrong":["Leto","Vesna","Osen'"]},{"id":"aa85a06f2a34","q":"When was the Declaration of Independence approved by the Second Continental Congress?","correct":"July 4, 1776","wrong":["May 4, 1776","June 4, 1776","July 2, 1776"]},{"id":"f948f2bf48b2","q":"Which product did Nokia, the telecommunications company, originally sell?","correct":"Paper","wrong":["Phones","Computers","Processors"]},{"id":"8c3775b041b2","q":"Which American president appears on a one dollar bill?","correct":"George Washington","wrong":["Thomas Jefferson","Abraham Lincoln","Benjamin Franklin"]},{"id":"5a55d5044c11","q":"Which church's interior in Vatican City was designed in 1503 by renaissance architects including Bramante, Michelangelo and Bernini?","correct":"St. Peter's Basilica","wrong":["Catania Cathedral","St. Mark’s Basilica","The Duomo of Florence"]},{"id":"9c3fee9ff136","q":"Which company did Valve cooperate with in the creation of the Vive?","correct":"HTC","wrong":["Oculus","Google","Razer"]},{"id":"d6c43a6bceaa","q":"If a person's hair is described as 'Titian', what colour is it?","correct":"Red","wrong":["Blonde","Brunette","Black"]},{"id":"0e5e4d2bd8e0","q":"Linus Pauling, one of the only winners of multiple Nobel Prizes, earned his Nobel Prizes in Chemistry and what?","correct":"Peace","wrong":["Physics","Economics","Physiology/Medicine"]},{"id":"60c17e7f2f0d","q":"Nephelococcygia is the practice of doing what?","correct":"Finding shapes in clouds","wrong":["Sleeping with your eyes open","Breaking glass with your voice","Swimming in freezing water"]},{"id":"f8379888d993","q":"What is the Swedish word for \"window\"?","correct":"Fönster","wrong":["H&aring;l","Skärm","Ruta"]},{"id":"b59317b03fcc","q":"What do sailors call the left side of a boat?","correct":"Port","wrong":["Starboard","Bow","Stern"]},{"id":"2a3fe9332c21","q":"Which of the following nations was NOT a belligerent in World War I?","correct":"Denmark","wrong":["Portugal","Greece","Romania"]},{"id":"5f73d1ec4d8d","q":"Five dollars is worth how many nickels?","correct":"100","wrong":["50","25","69"]},{"id":"f9b62a94344a","q":"What does the \"G\" mean in \"G-Man\"?","correct":"Government","wrong":["Going","Ghost","Geronimo"]},{"id":"4fb7238086f0","q":"In which cardinal direction does the Sun rise from?","correct":"East","wrong":["West","North","South"]},{"id":"554e6727c86e","q":"What was the name of Sqiudward's bad painting in the Spongebob episode \"Artist Unknown?\"","correct":"Bold and Brash","wrong":["Squidward en Repose","Rippy Bits","Tilted Perspectives"]},{"id":"7f1958804a19","q":"What type of dog is 'Handsome Dan', the mascot of Yale University?","correct":"Bulldog","wrong":["Yorkshire Terrier","Boxer","Pug"]},{"id":"aa3b51a82322","q":"What year was the first Apple iPod introduced?","correct":"2001","wrong":["2000","1999","1998"]},{"id":"a6d04e57ea62","q":"If you are caught \"Goldbricking\", what are you doing wrong?","correct":"Slacking","wrong":["Smoking","Stealing","Cheating"]},{"id":"6be57f0a45bc","q":"What do sailors call the back of a boat?","correct":"Stern","wrong":["Bow","Starboard","Port"]},{"id":"4ce9be789cd1","q":"De Eemhof, Port Zelande and Het Heijderbos are holiday villas owned by what company?","correct":"Center Parcs","wrong":["Yelloh Village","Keycamp","Villa Plus"]},{"id":"9e93ff05f7e4","q":"The early part of which decade, did the Goth Subculture begin?","correct":"1980s","wrong":["1990s","2000s","1970s"]},{"id":"22155d8d4f9d","q":"What is on display in the Madame Tussaud's museum in London?","correct":"Wax sculptures","wrong":["Designer clothing","Unreleased film reels","Vintage cars"]},{"id":"ea95ca539eff","q":"Which canal connects the Mediterranean Sea with the Red Sea?","correct":"Suez Canal","wrong":["Panama Canal","Sinai Canal","Qaraqum Canal"]},{"id":"c84cc6b4c53f","q":"Which of the following blood component forms a plug at the site of injuries?","correct":"Platelets","wrong":["Red blood cells","White blood cells","Blood plasma"]},{"id":"edd7bcb3af25","q":"What is the name of the extra pedal on a manual or standard transmission car?","correct":"Clutch","wrong":["Shifter","Booster","Parking Brake"]},{"id":"9e782f98c1eb","q":"Which of the following landmarks is not located in New York City?","correct":"Lincoln Memorial","wrong":["Empire State Building","Times Square","Central Park"]},{"id":"75dde8bc875a","q":"How tall is the Burj Khalifa?","correct":"2,722 ft","wrong":["2,717 ft","2,546 ft","3,024 ft"]},{"id":"4f071af8f3a6","q":"What is the name of the main Character from the Series: Dead Space?","correct":"Isaac Clarke","wrong":["Ellen Ripley","Commander Shepard","Captain Kirk"]},{"id":"baeb0dece005","q":"What is the currency of Poland?","correct":"Złoty","wrong":["Ruble","Euro","Krone"]},{"id":"e1aea39af535","q":"Out of these four buildings, which one is the tallest, with a height of 1,250 ft (381 m)?","correct":"Empire State Building, United States","wrong":["Bank of China Tower, Hong Kong","Federation Tower, Russia","Gevora Hotal, United Arab Emirates"]},{"id":"e8288bbd40fa","q":"The Mexican Beer \"Corona\" is what type of beer?","correct":"Pale Lager","wrong":["India Pale Ale","Pilfsner","Baltic Porter"]},{"id":"229268059706","q":"According to the nursery rhyme, what fruit did Little Jack Horner pull out of his Christmas pie?","correct":"Plum","wrong":["Apple","Peach","Pear"]},{"id":"52a32a495125","q":"According to the 2014-2015 Australian Bureau of Statistics, what percentage of Australians were born overseas?","correct":"28%","wrong":["13%","20%","7%"]},{"id":"6e7e4bbba10d","q":"This Ghanaian entrepreneur is a pioneer of microlending.","correct":"Esther Afua Ocloo","wrong":["Farida Bedwei","Ama Ata Aido","Sionne Neely"]},{"id":"90c224f4089c","q":"What do sailors call the front of a boat?","correct":"Bow","wrong":["Stern","Port","Starboard"]},{"id":"c13b9c5efa5f","q":"What does a milliner make and sell?","correct":"Hats","wrong":["Shoes","Belts","Shirts"]},{"id":"98f49ba7bb8a","q":"What is the first book of the Old Testament?","correct":"Genesis","wrong":["Exodus","Leviticus","Numbers"]},{"id":"6f8f1291563b","q":"The website \"Shut Up & Sit Down\" reviews which form of media?","correct":"Board Games","wrong":["Television Shows","Video Games","Films"]},{"id":"51fd5298248c","q":"Where is Apple Inc. headquartered?","correct":"Cupertino, California","wrong":["Redwood City, California","Redmond, Washington","Santa Monica, CA"]},{"id":"63ce45ab8e9d","q":"In blood typing, the (+) and (-) marker after an A, B, AB, or O is called Rh factor. Which of the following is the source of its discovery?","correct":"Rhesus Monkeys","wrong":["Rheumatism Patients","Red-Haired People","Rhizomes"]},{"id":"84a13878e6ba","q":"Who is the origin of the quote \"What doesn't kill you makes you stronger\"?","correct":"Friedrich Nietzsche","wrong":["G. Gordon Liddy","Kelly Clarkson","Christopher Hitchens"]},{"id":"4c6b147eec3b","q":"Which of the following card games revolves around numbers and basic math?","correct":"Uno","wrong":["Go Fish","Twister","Munchkin"]},{"id":"443c311cc879","q":"Which iconic Disneyland attraction was closed in 2017 to be remodeled as a \"Guardians of the Galaxy\" themed ride?","correct":"Twilight Zone Tower of Terror","wrong":["The Haunted Mansion","Pirates of the Caribbean","Peter Pan's Flight"]},{"id":"dac90d6b90cd","q":"What is the closest planet to our solar system's sun?","correct":"Mercury","wrong":["Mars","Jupiter","Earth"]},{"id":"ea68f2ae6881","q":"Who is a co-founder of music streaming service Spotify?","correct":"Daniel Ek","wrong":["Sean Parker","Felix Miller","Michael Breidenbruecker"]},{"id":"58c7ca950649","q":"What is the name of the currency used in Ethiopia?","correct":"Birr","wrong":["Dirham","U.S. Dollar","Rand"]},{"id":"182b9c47cad9","q":"Which country, not including Japan, has the most people of Japanese descent?","correct":"Brazil","wrong":["China","South Korea","United States of America"]},{"id":"80f1aeb5e882","q":"Which Italian automobile manufacturer gained majority control of U.S. automobile manufacturer Chrysler in 2011?","correct":"Fiat","wrong":["Maserati","Alfa Romeo","Ferrari"]},{"id":"b4a367aea602","q":"Which of the three astronauts of the Apollo 11 spaceflight did NOT walk on the moon?","correct":"Michael Collins","wrong":["Buzz Aldrin","Neil Armstrong","None of them"]},{"id":"29af1beeac96","q":"When was WhatsApp founded?","correct":"2009","wrong":["2007","2012","2010"]},{"id":"cb951ccaf0e6","q":"What is the shape of the toy invented by Hungarian professor Ernő Rubik?","correct":"Cube","wrong":["Sphere","Cylinder","Pyramid"]},{"id":"4ab2fc107bfc","q":"Which of these Nicktoons were NOT originally a short on Oh Yeah! Cartoons before becoming their own series?","correct":"Danny Phantom","wrong":["ChalkZone","My Life as a Teenage Robot","The Fairly OddParents"]},{"id":"0158c998c587","q":"Waluigi's first appearance was in what game?","correct":"Mario Tennis 64 (N64)","wrong":["Wario Land: Super Mario Land 3","Mario Party (N64)","Super Smash Bros. Ultimate"]},{"id":"2ab348c571e6","q":"What is a Burgee?","correct":"A flag","wrong":["A rope","A window","A type of food"]},{"id":"a36dc66335a1","q":"Of the following months, which has the most amount of days?","correct":"December","wrong":["April","September","November"]}],"science":[{"id":"d831dfb13935","q":"This element, when overcome with extreme heat and pressure, creates diamonds.","correct":"Carbon","wrong":["Nitrogen","Oxygen","Hydrogen"]},{"id":"0d066e528eb9","q":"Who discovered the Law of Gravity?","correct":"Sir Isaac Newton","wrong":["Galileo Galilei","Charles Darwin","Albert Einstein"]},{"id":"de0e7af4dc5e","q":"What is the colour of unoxidized blood?","correct":"Red","wrong":["Blue","Purple","Green"]},{"id":"c43d4e1468bd","q":"What is Hypernatremia?","correct":"Increase in blood sodium","wrong":["Decrease in blood potassium","Increase in blood glucose","Decrease in blood iron"]},{"id":"2d0d2063645d","q":"Which of these is NOT a bone found in the human arm?","correct":"Tibia","wrong":["Humerus","Ulna","Radius"]},{"id":"57e8f40a8cf5","q":"The medial meniscus forms which part of what joint in the human body?","correct":"Knee","wrong":["Elbow","Ankle","Shoulder"]},{"id":"7ea2141bf33b","q":"What produces the green colour of most plant leaves?","correct":"Chlorophyll","wrong":["Light refraction","Natural pigments","UV radiation"]},{"id":"c84c5781c3d2","q":"The medical condition osteoporosis affects which part of the body?","correct":"Bones","wrong":["Skin","Brain","Heart"]},{"id":"67a0b0da1247","q":"Which type of rock is created by intense heat AND pressure?","correct":"Metamorphic","wrong":["Sedimentary","Igneous","Diamond"]},{"id":"e9e2cddf5c67","q":"What is the Linnean name of the domestic apple tree?","correct":"Malus pumila","wrong":["Malus americana","Pomus domestica","Appelus delectica"]},{"id":"8f2e68958907","q":"What organelle aids in synthesis of DNA in cells?","correct":"Ribosomes","wrong":["Nuclei","Lysosomes","Mitochondria"]},{"id":"853df87c6e92","q":"Myopia is the scientific term for which condition?","correct":"Shortsightedness","wrong":["Farsightedness","Double Vision","Clouded Vision"]},{"id":"803ab3be203f","q":"Botanically speaking, which of these fruits is NOT a berry?","correct":"Strawberry","wrong":["Blueberry","Banana","Concord Grape"]},{"id":"85bd4e31e75f","q":"Which NASA Space Shuttle broke apart during atmospheric re-entry on February 1, 2003?","correct":"Columbia","wrong":["Challenger","Discovery","Endeavour"]},{"id":"722d4712703f","q":"When was the first mammal successfully cloned?","correct":"1996","wrong":["2009","1999","1985"]},{"id":"a40cf6393ca1","q":"What is the standard SI unit for temperature?","correct":"Kelvin","wrong":["Fahrenheit","Celsius","Rankine"]},{"id":"4f3856d70db1","q":"How many planets are in our Solar System?","correct":"Eight","wrong":["Nine","Seven","Ten"]},{"id":"2abe1ae31868","q":"The \"Tibia\" is found in which part of the body?","correct":"Leg","wrong":["Arm","Hand","Head"]},{"id":"cf414a514eba","q":"What did Gregory Mendel use to test genetic crossovers?","correct":"Peas","wrong":["Cats","Flowers","Parrots"]},{"id":"8e731ed0cca8","q":"Folic acid is the synthetic form of which vitamin?","correct":"Vitamin B","wrong":["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin D"]},{"id":"595069994e84","q":"How many baby/milk teeth does a human child have in total?","correct":"20","wrong":["10","15","25"]},{"id":"10e8df5a9f5f","q":"What is the unit of electrical capacitance?","correct":"Farad","wrong":["Gauss","Henry","Watt"]},{"id":"93a4506cb82d","q":"What does DNA stand for?","correct":"Deoxyribonucleic Acid","wrong":["Deoxyribogenetic Acid","Deoxyribogenetic Atoms","Detoxic Acid"]},{"id":"4bedf10d05cb","q":"Which chemical element has the lowest boiling point?","correct":"Helium","wrong":["Hydrogen","Neon","Nitrogen"]},{"id":"fc81ae43efba","q":"What is the chemical makeup of water?","correct":"H20","wrong":["C12H6O2","CO2","H"]},{"id":"c4e955cb4e9c","q":"Which of the following plastic is commonly used for window frames, gutters and drain pipes?","correct":"Polyvinylchloride (PVC)","wrong":["Polyethylene (PE)","Polypropylene (PP)","Polystyrene (PS)"]},{"id":"d5e58b931bb7","q":"What is the largest living organism currently known to man?","correct":"Honey Fungus","wrong":["Blue Whale","Redwood Tree","The Coral Reef"]},{"id":"94c582e8baf0","q":"On the Beaufort Scale of wind force, what wind name is given to number 8?","correct":"Gale","wrong":["Storm","Hurricane","Breeze"]},{"id":"22d3158f49e0","q":"The biggest distinction between a eukaryotic cell and a prokaryotic cell is:","correct":"The presence or absence of a nucleus","wrong":["The overall size","The presence or absence of certain organelles","The mode of reproduction"]},{"id":"b2ee06449142","q":"Which of these bones is hardest to break?","correct":"Femur","wrong":["Cranium","Humerus","Tibia"]},{"id":"b88e6f98150a","q":"How many legs is it biologically impossible for a centipede to have?","correct":"100","wrong":["26","50","74"]},{"id":"43d07331b242","q":"Coulrophobia is the irrational fear of what?","correct":"Clowns","wrong":["Cemeteries","Needles","Tunnels"]},{"id":"26d17c5ed1b9","q":"What is the chemical symbol for lead?","correct":"Pb","wrong":["Ld","Le","Pm"]},{"id":"67851c3ab786","q":"Autosomal-dominant Compelling Helio-Ophthalmic Outburst syndrome is the need to do what when seeing the Sun?","correct":"Sneeze","wrong":["Cough","Yawn","Hiccup"]},{"id":"f72f8ac38254","q":"What is the elemental symbol for mercury?","correct":"Hg","wrong":["Me","Mc","Hy"]},{"id":"7e18622fbcca","q":"What is the scientific name for the extinct hominin known as \"Lucy\"?","correct":"Australopithecus Afarensis","wrong":["Australopithecus Africanus","Australopithecus Architeuthis","Australopithecus Antaris"]},{"id":"0a07be81c159","q":"Who made the discovery of X-rays?","correct":"Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen","wrong":["Thomas Alva Edison","James Watt","Albert Einstein"]},{"id":"65a2dd06febb","q":"How many planets make up our Solar System?","correct":"8","wrong":["7","9","6"]},{"id":"de05405af051","q":"Where is the Gluteus Maximus muscle located?","correct":"Butt","wrong":["Arm","Head","Torso"]},{"id":"a2e1453ecfa2","q":"What is the unit of electrical resistance?","correct":"Ohm","wrong":["Mho","Tesla","Joule"]},{"id":"138e66648274","q":"How many laws of thermodynamics are there?","correct":"Four","wrong":["Three","Two","Five"]},{"id":"dc86e883c08d","q":"What is the speed of light in a vacuum?","correct":"299,792,458 m/s","wrong":["50,461 m/s","308,215,043 m/s","751,665,014,151 m/s"]},{"id":"25cc61ed7d10","q":"Which of the following liquids is least viscous? Assume temperature is 25&deg;C.","correct":"Acetone","wrong":["Water","Mercury","Benzene"]},{"id":"7796fe01c358","q":"How many officially recognized dwarf planets in the solar system are named after Polynesian deities?","correct":"2","wrong":["0","1","5"]},{"id":"b984e3ca0d63","q":"What is an alternative name for multiple personality disorder?","correct":"Dissociative identity disorder","wrong":["Body integrity identity disorder","Identity crisis","Schizophrenia"]},{"id":"60dafa95557d","q":"Which color cannot be produced in Roses, even through genetic alteration?","correct":"Blue","wrong":["Black","Orange","Brown"]},{"id":"826ff8dfb243","q":"The core of the Sun can reach which temperature?","correct":"27&deg; Million F (15&deg; Million C)","wrong":["938,000&deg; F (521093.3&deg; C)","8&deg; Billion F (&deg;4.4 Billion C)","Absolute Zero (Both F and C)"]},{"id":"3fd1d3dcafa2","q":"Which is the longest bone in the human body?","correct":"Femur","wrong":["Scapula","Fibula","Ulna"]},{"id":"70319dcf51d9","q":"Which of these stars is the largest?","correct":"UY Scuti","wrong":["VY Canis Majoris","Betelgeuse","RW Cephei"]},{"id":"d1577605ce9d","q":"What is the name for the auditory illusion of a note that seems to be rising infinitely?","correct":"Shepard Tone","wrong":["Glissandro Illusion","Fransen Effect","McGurck Effect"]},{"id":"833fa387ff63","q":"About what percentage of the Earth's surface is water?","correct":"70%","wrong":["30%","50%","90%"]},{"id":"d52b0f61e303","q":"What do you study if you are studying entomology?","correct":"Insects","wrong":["Humans","the Brain","Fish"]},{"id":"2a2880673d67","q":"What part of the brain takes its name from the Greek for seahorse?","correct":"Hippocampus","wrong":["Cerebellum","Thalamus","Amygdala"]},{"id":"5c46f7913261","q":"How many planets are there in the Solar System?","correct":"8","wrong":["9","11","10"]},{"id":"35b1d16ce5c5","q":"Which Apollo mission was the first one to land on the Moon?","correct":"Apollo 11","wrong":["Apollo 10","Apollo 9","Apollo 13"]},{"id":"582392b874a2","q":"Which of the following are cells of the adaptive immune system?","correct":"Cytotoxic T cells","wrong":["Dendritic cells","Natural killer cells","White blood cells"]},{"id":"9182056a467e","q":"How many protons are in an oxygen atom?","correct":"Eight","wrong":["Four","Two","Six"]},{"id":"d72ff8a15ca4","q":"What is the standard SI unit for distance?","correct":"Metre","wrong":["Angstrom","Foot","Fathom"]},{"id":"e1459503e285","q":"Which gas forms about 78% of the Earth’s atmosphere?","correct":"Nitrogen","wrong":["Oxygen","Argon","Carbon Dioxide"]},{"id":"a8eea229be4f","q":"The moons, Miranda, Ariel, Umbriel, Titania and Oberon orbit which planet?","correct":"Uranus","wrong":["Jupiter","Venus","Neptune"]},{"id":"945b58f05c9d","q":"All the following metal elements are liquids at or near room temperature EXCEPT:","correct":"Beryllium","wrong":["Gallium","Caesium","Mercury"]},{"id":"9b78628af885","q":"What nucleotide pairs with guanine?","correct":"Cytosine","wrong":["Thymine","Adenine","Uracil"]},{"id":"af155a1c9777","q":"71% of the Earth's surface is made up of","correct":"Water","wrong":["Deserts","Continents","Forests"]},{"id":"76a55ef94e2f","q":"What animal takes part in Schrödinger's most famous thought experiment?","correct":"Cat","wrong":["Dog","Bat","Butterfly"]},{"id":"fd111a84b619","q":"Approximately how long is a year on Uranus?","correct":"84 Earth years","wrong":["47 Earth years","62 Earth years","109 Earth years"]},{"id":"b90db676a5f1","q":"Which of the following is the male pollen-producing reproductive part of a flower?","correct":"Stamen","wrong":["Sepal","Pistil","Petal"]},{"id":"00efd0b6e884","q":"What is the standard atomic weight of a Plutonium nucleus?","correct":"244","wrong":["94","481","128"]},{"id":"11573a63f243","q":"Which portion of the Marijuana plant produces the psychoactive substance known as THC?","correct":"Female Flower","wrong":["Leaves","Male Flower","Root Ball"]},{"id":"d8117c67fa6e","q":"On which mission did the Space Shuttle Columbia break up upon re-entry?","correct":"STS-107","wrong":["STS-51-L","STS-61-C","STS-109"]},{"id":"6e36c463f06b","q":"How many moons does Pluto have?","correct":"Five","wrong":["Two","Three","One"]},{"id":"8318eb1d0c37","q":"What does the scientific name of the Cambrian-Period sea creature Anomalocaris mean?","correct":"Abnormal Shrimp","wrong":["Deformed Fish","Strange Crab","Anomalous Clam"]},{"id":"8810fca19839","q":"Which is the most abundant element in the universe?","correct":"Hydrogen","wrong":["Helium","Lithium","Oxygen"]},{"id":"99102548e48e","q":"What physics principle relates the net electric flux out of a closed surface to the charge enclosed by that surface?","correct":"Gauss's Law","wrong":["Faraday's Law","Ampere's Law","Biot-Savart Law"]},{"id":"abe981f91c27","q":"An organism described as \"heliotropic\" has a tendancy to move towards which of these things?","correct":"Light","wrong":["Water","Trees","Pollen"]},{"id":"786e84da9190","q":"What is the standard SI unit for luminous intensity?","correct":"Candela","wrong":["Lumen","Faraday","Coulomb"]},{"id":"77ae4059cceb","q":"What is the scientific name of the knee cap?","correct":"Patella","wrong":["Femur","Foramen Magnum","Scapula"]},{"id":"967cd0585b58","q":"In Psychology, which need appears highest in the \"Maslow's hierarchy of needs\" pyramid?","correct":"Esteem","wrong":["Love","Safety","Physiological"]},{"id":"91eaa5d74678","q":"Which Landsat Satellite currently has had the longest operational life?","correct":"Landsat 5","wrong":["Landsat 8","Landsat 7","Landsat 6"]},{"id":"9efb56926c9b","q":"When the Falcon Heavy was launched on it's test flight, what was the only part of the operation that failed?","correct":"Center Core Landing","wrong":["Side Booster Landing","Deployment of Starman","Ignition and Liftoff"]},{"id":"d163b0781b69","q":"What is the same in Celsius and Fahrenheit?","correct":"-40","wrong":["32","-39","-42"]},{"id":"4fee8aa14595","q":"After which Danish city is the 72th element on the periodic table named?","correct":"Copenhagen","wrong":["Odense","Herning","Skagen"]},{"id":"6c0d97b55950","q":"What is the lowest layer of the Earth's atmosphere named?","correct":"Troposphere","wrong":["Stratosphere","Mesosphere","Thermosphere"]},{"id":"dc3864cfc730","q":"An organic compound is considered an alcohol if it has what functional group?","correct":"Hydroxyl","wrong":["Carbonyl","Alkyl","Aldehyde"]},{"id":"fca028b8f2fa","q":"The Western Lowland Gorilla is scientifically know as?","correct":"Gorilla Gorilla Gorilla","wrong":["Gorilla Gorilla Diehli","Gorilla Beringei Graueri","Gorilla Beringei Beringei"]},{"id":"d5ccf106ae14","q":"Approximately what percentage of Earth's atmosphere is Oxygen?","correct":"21%","wrong":["54%","78%","7%"]},{"id":"974250ab0d78","q":"A positron is an antiparticle of a what?","correct":"Electron","wrong":["Neutron","Proton","Photon"]},{"id":"f4f777875e10","q":"What term is best associated with Sigmund Freud?","correct":"Psychoanalysis","wrong":["Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy","Theory of Gravity","Dialectical Behavior Therapy"]},{"id":"878fc1cc731c","q":"\"The Big Bang Theory\" was first theorized by a priest of what religious ideology?","correct":"Catholic","wrong":["Christian","Jewish","Islamic"]},{"id":"8f63494f665e","q":"How many moons does the Earth have?","correct":"1","wrong":["0","2","3"]},{"id":"affba3d18dea","q":"What is the chemical formula for ammonia?","correct":"NH3","wrong":["CO2","NO3","CH4"]},{"id":"356ef3130e36","q":"Which is the chemical name of H2O?","correct":"Dihydrogen Monoxide","wrong":["Ammonium chloride","Anhydrous Sodium Carbonate","Manganese dioxide"]},{"id":"efb8f1be7068","q":"Which psychological term refers to the stress of holding contrasting beliefs?","correct":"Cognitive Dissonance","wrong":["Flip-Flop Syndrome","Split-Brain","Blind Sight"]},{"id":"ecf00315defa","q":"Which major extinction event was caused by an asteroid collision and eliminated the majority of non-avian dinosaurs?","correct":"Cretaceous-Paleogene","wrong":["Triassic–Jurassic","Permian–Triassic","Ordovician–Silurian"]},{"id":"9bd3183d705d","q":"Which planet in the Solar System is the closest to the Sun?","correct":"Mercury","wrong":["Earth","Mars","Venus"]},{"id":"51f61da3d9eb","q":"Which continent do sweet potatoes originally come from?","correct":"South America","wrong":["Asia","Africa","Europe"]},{"id":"cc21c31d8527","q":"Which is not a type of neuron?","correct":"Perceptual Neuron","wrong":["Sensory Neuron","Motor Neuron","Interneuron"]},{"id":"69e9cb763efd","q":"The asteroid belt is located between which two planets?","correct":"Mars and Jupiter","wrong":["Jupiter and Saturn","Mercury and Venus","Earth and Mars"]},{"id":"ae348676b300","q":"How many teeth does the average adult mouth have (except for wisdom teeth)?","correct":"32","wrong":["36","20","28"]},{"id":"988e30803129","q":"Which of the following blood vessels carries deoxygenated blood?","correct":"Pulmonary Artery","wrong":["Pulmonary Vein","Aorta","Coronary Artery"]},{"id":"78d74d79ac3a","q":"What does the term \"isolation\" refer to in microbiology?","correct":"The separation of a strain from a natural, mixed population of living microbes","wrong":["A lack of nutrition in microenviroments","The nitrogen level in soil","Testing effects of certain microorganisms in an isolated enviroments, such as caves"]},{"id":"42ec0d33ebb9","q":"Which scientific unit is named after an Italian nobleman?","correct":"Volt","wrong":["Pascal","Ohm","Hertz"]},{"id":"a7a642f51817","q":"What is the hottest planet in the solar system","correct":"Venus","wrong":["Jupiter","Mercury","Mars"]},{"id":"06dffd6fdcc8","q":"Which planet did the \"Viking 1\" spacecraft send surface images of, starting in 1976?","correct":"Mars","wrong":["Saturn","Jupiter","Venus"]},{"id":"9e2b8b918b96","q":"What is the molecular formula of Glucose?","correct":"C6H12O6","wrong":["C2H4O2","K+","CH4"]},{"id":"1fc71f0744de","q":"What is the largest planet in the Solar System?","correct":"Jupiter","wrong":["Saturn","Earth","Mars"]},{"id":"c2262c53f001","q":"The Axiom of Preventive Medicine states that people with ___ risk for a disease should be screened and we should treat ___ of those people.","correct":"low, all","wrong":["low, some","high, all","high, some"]},{"id":"7a08b7408e8e","q":"What was the category of the 2005 hurricane, Hurricane Katrina, in the Saffir-Simpson hurricane wind scale?","correct":"Category 5","wrong":["Category 1","Category 4","Category 2"]},{"id":"a9a2863a6991","q":"Which of the following men does not have a chemical element named after him?","correct":"Sir Isaac Newton","wrong":["Albert Einstein","Niels Bohr","Enrico Fermi"]},{"id":"5585e908ac17","q":"What name is given to all baby marsupials?","correct":"Joey","wrong":["Calf","Pup","Cub"]},{"id":"efc7848d79e8","q":"What is isobutylphenylpropanoic acid more commonly known as?","correct":"Ibuprofen","wrong":["Morphine","Ketamine","Aspirin"]},{"id":"804bef5f5f82","q":"What is the scientific name of the red fox?","correct":"Vulpes Vulpes","wrong":["Vulpes Redus","Red Fox","Vulpes Vulpie"]},{"id":"bdc0da9e91fe","q":"In aeronautics, flaps and slats are used to control what on an aircraft?","correct":"Lift","wrong":["Thrust","Drag","Weight"]},{"id":"d576051bf4f1","q":"Deuterium is an isotope of which element?","correct":"Hydrogen","wrong":["Nitrogen","Helium","Neon"]},{"id":"73bf89363ab1","q":"Which element has the chemical symbol 'Fe'?","correct":"Iron","wrong":["Gold","Silver","Tin"]},{"id":"799b6147200d","q":"What is the name of the Supermassive Black Hole in the centre of the Milky Way?","correct":"Sagittarius A*","wrong":["Messier 87","Alpha Centauri","Andromeda"]},{"id":"32643a3d0357","q":"The humerus, paired radius, and ulna come together to form what joint?","correct":"Elbow","wrong":["Knee","Sholder","Ankle"]},{"id":"7ecba96837ec","q":"Which Swiss psychologist is synonymous with the concepts of introvert and extrovert personalities?","correct":"Carl Jung","wrong":["Jean Piaget","Alice Miller","Hermann Rorschach"]},{"id":"56533f799e30","q":"Which of these two plates are best know for forming earthquakes and tsunami's?","correct":"Convergent Plate Boundaries/Oceanic Crust","wrong":["Divergent Plate Boundaries/Convergent/Oceanic Crust","Transform Plate Boundaries/Divergent Plate Boundaries","Oceanic & Continental Crust/Transform Plate Boundaries"]},{"id":"6b76b196bb72","q":"Muscle fiber is constructed of bundles small long organelles called what?","correct":"Myofibrils","wrong":["Epimysium","Myofiaments","Myocardium"]},{"id":"853b22f01d1f","q":"What is the medical term for low blood sugar?","correct":"Hypoglycemia","wrong":["Hypothyroidism","Hypothermia","Hypoxia"]},{"id":"698cc5533d1a","q":"The Sun consists of mostly which two elements?","correct":"Hydrogen & Helium","wrong":["Hydrogen & Nitrogen","Carbon & Nitrogen","Carbon & Helium"]},{"id":"3add785e6826","q":"What common name is given to the medial condition, tibial stress syndrome (MTSS)?","correct":"Shin Splints","wrong":["Tennis Elbow","Carpal Tunnel","Housemaid's Knee"]},{"id":"1e395bf8b7ad","q":"Which of these is a semiconductor amplifying device?","correct":"transistor","wrong":["tube","diode","P-N junction"]},{"id":"a9861755181f","q":"Which element has the atomic number of 7?","correct":"Nitrogen","wrong":["Oxygen","Hydrogen","Neon"]},{"id":"79d8caf44299","q":"In human biology, a circadium rhythm relates to a period of roughly how many hours?","correct":"24","wrong":["8","16","32"]},{"id":"87531afbdacc","q":"What is the unit of electrical inductance?","correct":"Henry","wrong":["Weber","Coulomb","Mho"]},{"id":"25c4d6db63b7","q":"Which element has the highest melting point?","correct":"Carbon","wrong":["Tungsten","Platinum","Osmium"]},{"id":"eca66171093f","q":"Which one of these scientists conducted the Gold Foil Experiment which concluded that atoms are mostly made of empty space?","correct":"Ernest Rutherford","wrong":["Joseph John Thomson","Archimedes","Niels Henrik David Bohr"]},{"id":"73b8c9009b98","q":"What are the smallest blood vessels in the human body?","correct":"Capillaries","wrong":["Arterioles","Veinules","Lymphatics"]},{"id":"2f30e3afc5d6","q":"Which of these is a type of stretch/deep tendon reflex?","correct":"Ankle jerk reflex","wrong":["Gag reflex","Pupillary light reflex","Scratch reflex"]},{"id":"4dd1146cebd5","q":"How many bones are in the human body?","correct":"206","wrong":["203","209","200"]},{"id":"a6ead263418d","q":"The human right lung has how many lobes?","correct":"3","wrong":["4","2","1"]},{"id":"d9c3f562fbe6","q":"Burning which of these metals will produce a bright white flame?","correct":"Magnesium","wrong":["Copper","Lithium","Lead"]},{"id":"85cae6cca9e4","q":"Which one of these is scientific term for \"Brain Freeze\"?","correct":"Sphenopalatine Ganglioneuralgia","wrong":["Hyacinthoides Italica","Amaranthus Retroflexus","Amblyomma Americanum"]},{"id":"6537dbb61c5a","q":"Which of the following bones is not in the leg?","correct":"Radius","wrong":["Patella","Tibia","Fibula"]},{"id":"18d48f9f2984","q":"What does LASER stand for?","correct":"Light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation","wrong":["Lite analysing by stereo ecorazer","Light amplifier by standby energy of radio","Life antimatter by standing entry of range"]},{"id":"75cb5382ea88","q":"On the periodic table of elements, what is the symbol for Tin?","correct":"Sn","wrong":["Ti","Ni","Na"]},{"id":"516a35b4bdb3","q":"What is the most potent toxin known?","correct":"Botulinum toxin","wrong":["Ricin","Cyanide","Asbestos"]},{"id":"e41ca3ac4660","q":"Who is the chemical element Curium named after?","correct":"Marie & Pierre Curie","wrong":["The Curiosity Rover","Curious George","Stephen Curry"]},{"id":"57aac115b6c4","q":"A comet's gaseous envelope (which creates the tail) is called what?","correct":"The coma","wrong":["The wake","The backwash","The ablative"]},{"id":"cfea67841e4f","q":"What is \"Stenoma\"?","correct":"A genus of moths","wrong":["A combat stimulant from WW2","A type of seasoning","A port city in the carribean"]},{"id":"f588b5ce68de","q":"How many hearts does an octopus have?","correct":"Three","wrong":["One","Two","Four"]},{"id":"b6142f07f749","q":"What does CPR, the emergency procedure to assist someone who has suffered cardiac arrest, stand for?","correct":"Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","wrong":["Chronic pain relief","Cancer pain release","Contraceptive prevalence rate"]},{"id":"45a208d8b544","q":"Rhinoplasty is a surgical procedure on what part of the human body?","correct":"Nose","wrong":["Ears","Chin","Neck"]},{"id":"04de47668137","q":"Which of these chemical compounds is NOT found in gastric acid?","correct":"Sulfuric acid","wrong":["Hydrochloric acid","Potassium chloride","Sodium chloride"]},{"id":"fc1c16b1679a","q":"In the Scoville scale, what is the hottest chemical?","correct":"Resiniferatoxin","wrong":["Capsaicin","Dihydrocapsaicin","Tinyatoxin"]},{"id":"90ab80ee4a4b","q":"Which of the following is NOT a passive electrical component?","correct":"Transistor","wrong":["Resistor","Capacitor","Inductor"]},{"id":"2eec8a82dba5","q":"What is the standard SI unit for electric current?","correct":"Ampere","wrong":["Volt","Ohm","Watt"]},{"id":"1f1048ee962e","q":"What is the atomic mass of Carbon?","correct":"12","wrong":["14","16","10"]},{"id":"4665a342827f","q":"What is the study of the cells and tissues of plants and animals?","correct":"Histology","wrong":["Microbiology","Anatomy","Biochemistry"]},{"id":"254e773bb7db","q":"What is the molecular formula of the active component of chili peppers(Capsaicin)?","correct":"C18H27NO3","wrong":["C21H23NO3","C6H4Cl2","C13H25NO4"]},{"id":"4cfba92475af","q":"Tetsuya Fujita was a scientist that developed the scale for which natural disaster?","correct":"Tornadoes","wrong":["Hurricanes","Earthquakes","Volcanoes"]},{"id":"1f568bd0b07f","q":"What is the half-life of Uranium-235?","correct":"703,800,000 years","wrong":["4,300,400,000 years","1,260,900,000 years","Uranium-235 is a stable isotope"]},{"id":"318d872d11b7","q":"Who developed the first successful polio vaccine in the 1950s?","correct":"Jonas Salk","wrong":["John F. Enders","Thomas Weller","Frederick Robbins"]},{"id":"9cd74818395e","q":"What lies at the center of our galaxy?","correct":"A black hole","wrong":["A wormhole","A supernova","A quasar"]},{"id":"a0f4a4f7ef54","q":"What medication was once commonly used as rat poison?","correct":"Coumadin","wrong":["Aspirin","Eliquis","Tylenol"]},{"id":"c55ce160d8b5","q":"What is the standard SI unit for mass?","correct":"Kilogram","wrong":["Tonne","Pound","Gram"]},{"id":"645b5adb1e53","q":"Which desert is the only desert in the world where the \"Saguaro\" cactus grows indigenously?","correct":"The Sonoran Desert","wrong":["The Gobi Desert","The Yuma Desert","The Arabian Desert"]},{"id":"21ded1ee65f3","q":"The 'Islets of Langerhans' is found in which human organ?","correct":"Pancreas","wrong":["Kidney","Liver","Brain"]},{"id":"b1328d61bbb4","q":"Human cells typically have how many copies of each gene?","correct":"2","wrong":["1","4","3"]},{"id":"83acef931a60","q":"How old is the universe?","correct":"13.8 Billion Years","wrong":["4.5 Billion Years","7.9 Billion Years","16.2 Billion Years"]},{"id":"6c1fb8d4e4e3","q":"Which horizon in a soil profile consists of bedrock?","correct":"R","wrong":["O","B","D"]},{"id":"52f16a01e702","q":"What is the thin, outermost layer of the Earth?","correct":"Crust","wrong":["Exosphere","Mantle","Outer Core"]},{"id":"a783717c8fc0","q":"What element on the periodic table has 92 electrons?","correct":"Uranium","wrong":["Sulfur","Hydrogen","Iron"]},{"id":"3108c23b928f","q":"What causes Lyme disease?","correct":"A bacteria","wrong":["A virus","A parasitic worm","An amoeba"]},{"id":"0c9ddbb99bca","q":"What is the mathematical formula of Ohm's law?","correct":"V = I*R","wrong":["I = V*R","R = V*I","V = I / R"]},{"id":"6d133b810703","q":"Alzheimer's disease primarily affects which part of the human body?","correct":"Brain","wrong":["Lungs","Skin","Heart"]},{"id":"31b4400b4d0f","q":"What is the chemical symbol for Helium?","correct":"He","wrong":["H","Hg","Hs"]},{"id":"39579d37febd","q":"How many objects are equivalent to one mole?","correct":"6.022 x 10^23","wrong":["6.002 x 10^22","6.022 x 10^22","6.002 x 10^23"]},{"id":"0f38c136d4e4","q":"Along with Oxygen, which element is primarily responsible for the sky appearing blue?","correct":"Nitrogen","wrong":["Helium","Carbon","Hydrogen"]},{"id":"004cff24bac7","q":"What is the powerhouse of the cell?","correct":"Mitochondria","wrong":["Ribosome","Redbull","Nucleus"]},{"id":"2e428ccda227","q":"Which part of the body does glaucoma affect?","correct":"Eyes","wrong":["Throat","Stomach","Blood"]},{"id":"d62c2fa41393","q":"What is the official name of the star located closest to the North Celestial Pole?","correct":"Polaris","wrong":["Eridanus","Gamma Cephei","Iota Cephei"]},{"id":"19d687428435","q":"What is the name of the cognitive bias wherein a person with low ability in a particular skill mistake themselves as being superior?","correct":"Dunning-Kruger effect","wrong":["Meyers-Briggs effect","Müller-Lyer effect","Freud-Hall effect"]},{"id":"5085f9e04c35","q":"Which country first successfully farm-hatched and raised bluefin tuna in 1979?","correct":"Japan","wrong":["France","USA","Philippines"]},{"id":"1ca4c4a86b01","q":"Which of the following is NOT a real element?","correct":"Vitrainium","wrong":["Praseodymium","Hassium","Lutetium"]},{"id":"b2f8bea8f7a1","q":"Gannymede is the largest moon of which planet?","correct":"Jupiter","wrong":["Uranus","Neptune","Mars"]},{"id":"699490a9c5c2","q":"Where in the human body is the Pineal Gland located?","correct":"Brain","wrong":["Groin","Chest","Throat"]},{"id":"f10e00754da6","q":"Which of the following is NOT a word used to describe an earthquake?","correct":"Drop-slide","wrong":["Foreshock","Strike-slip","Temblor"]},{"id":"fd1e496f8953","q":"Which of these is NOT a part of the structure of a typical neuron?","correct":"Islets of Langerhans","wrong":["Node of Ranvier","Schwann cell","Myelin sheath"]},{"id":"9e194e1fe97a","q":"How many types of quarks are there in the standard model of physics?","correct":"6","wrong":["2","3","4"]},{"id":"d7a23a206124","q":"What is the largest animal currently on Earth?","correct":"Blue Whale","wrong":["Orca","Colossal Squid","Giraffe"]},{"id":"1ca52207d362","q":"Which noble gas has the lowest atomic number?","correct":"Helium","wrong":["Neon","Argon","Krypton"]},{"id":"eb8088860de0","q":"What polymer is used to make CDs, safety goggles and riot shields?","correct":"Polycarbonate","wrong":["Rubber","Nylon","Bakelite"]},{"id":"f19a39c8db61","q":"What is the molecular formula of Ozone?","correct":"O3","wrong":["C6H2O6","N2O","SO4"]},{"id":"a435c3e87bd8","q":"How much radiation does a banana emit?","correct":"0.1 Microsievert","wrong":["0.3 Microsievert","0.5 Microsievert","0.7 Microsievert"]},{"id":"9586409060d3","q":"Dry ice is the solid form of what substance?","correct":"Carbon dioxide","wrong":["Nitrogen","Ammonia","Oxygen"]},{"id":"758a65a68741","q":"How many degrees Fahrenheit is 100 degrees Celsius?","correct":"212","wrong":["326","100","451"]},{"id":"0508b9f490bf","q":"If you planted the seeds of Quercus robur what would grow?","correct":"Trees","wrong":["Flowers","Vegtables","Grains"]},{"id":"c1263095ebbf","q":"Au on the Periodic Table refers to which element?","correct":"Gold","wrong":["Silver","Oxygen","Nickel"]},{"id":"faad975905d6","q":"Which of the following is considered classical conditioning?","correct":"Pavlov's dog experiments","wrong":["Skinner box experiment","Schrödinger's cat experiment","Harlow’s monkey experiments"]},{"id":"28261e362f6c","q":"Deionized water is water with which of the following removed?","correct":"Iron","wrong":["Oxygen","Hydrogen","Uncharged atoms"]},{"id":"d4f9494006ce","q":"In quantum physics, which of these theorised sub-atomic particles has yet to be observed?","correct":"Graviton","wrong":["Z boson","Tau neutrino","Gluon"]},{"id":"fc00b3914662","q":"Naturally occuring uranium primarily consists of which isotope?","correct":"238","wrong":["235","239","233"]},{"id":"3a7544ac560c","q":"What part of the body produces insulin?","correct":"Pancreas","wrong":["Kidney","Liver","Stomach"]},{"id":"5141ba0c1c0e","q":"What does the yellow diamond on the NFPA 704 fire diamond represent?","correct":"Reactivity","wrong":["Health","Flammability","Radioactivity"]},{"id":"b215e699b356","q":"To the nearest minute, how long does it take for light to travel from the Sun to the Earth?","correct":"8 Minutes","wrong":["6 Minutes","2 Minutes","12 Minutes"]},{"id":"27c3bc719225","q":"What is the \"powerhouse\" of the Eukaryotic animal cell?","correct":"Mitochondria","wrong":["Nucleus","Chloroplast","Endoplasmic Reticulum"]},{"id":"2950045c8508","q":"Which of the following spacecraft never touched the moon?","correct":"Mariner 4","wrong":["Apollo 11","Luna 2","SMART-1"]},{"id":"b40eefe3f3ae","q":"Which Landsat Satellite failed to reach orbit?","correct":"Landsat 6","wrong":["Landsat 5","Landsat 4","Landsat 3"]},{"id":"37a443bc81c8","q":"What is an example of a bacterial pathogen?","correct":"Cholera","wrong":["Measles","AIDS","Ringworm"]},{"id":"848b15290b65","q":"What is the standard SI unit for time?","correct":"Second","wrong":["Minute","Hour","Day"]},{"id":"45f521d1ca82","q":"What was the first organic compound to be synthesized from inorganic compounds?","correct":"Urea","wrong":["Propane","Ethanol","Formaldehyde"]},{"id":"e92edd62d9dd","q":"What are human nails made of?","correct":"Keratin","wrong":["Bone","Chitin","Calcium"]},{"id":"93fe929e5499","q":"What stage of development do the majority of eukaryotic cells remain in for most of their life?","correct":"Interphase","wrong":["Prophase","Stasis","Telophase"]},{"id":"dbd34c511fd1","q":"Which of the following is not one of the groups on the periodic table?","correct":"Fluorines","wrong":["Alkali Metals","Halogens","Noble Gases"]},{"id":"9fdf44eeb85f","q":"What is considered the rarest form of color blindness?","correct":"Blue","wrong":["Red","Green","Purple"]},{"id":"fde078d31dda","q":"What genetic disease is caused by having an extra Y chromosome (XYY)?","correct":"Jacob's Syndrome","wrong":["Klinefelter's Syndrome","Turner's Syndrome","Down Syndrome"]},{"id":"95a2f5dc5a2c","q":"What was the name of the first artificial Earth satellite, launched by the Soviet Union in 1957?","correct":"Sputnik 1","wrong":["Soyuz 7K-OK","Zenit-2","Voskhod 3KV"]},{"id":"3773a2a44514","q":"Which of these Elements is a metalloid?","correct":"Antimony","wrong":["Tin","Bromine","Rubidium"]},{"id":"befd2e793245","q":"What is the hottest planet in the Solar System?","correct":"Venus","wrong":["Mars","Mercury","Jupiter"]},{"id":"3d739727f924","q":"Which constellation contains the center of the Milky Way?","correct":"Sagittarius","wrong":["Scorpius","Ophiuchus","Capricornus"]},{"id":"62400505475b","q":"What cell organelle is known as \"the powerhouse of the cell?\"","correct":"Mitochondria","wrong":["Nucleus","Golgi apparatus","Endoplasmic reticulum"]},{"id":"d5e6ec5b3c06","q":"Which of the following is the term for \"surgical complications resulting from surgical sponges left inside the patient's body?","correct":"Gossypiboma","wrong":["Gongoozler","Jentacular","Meupareunia"]},{"id":"2f1c301f3e95","q":"Which of these animals belongs in class Chondrichthyes?","correct":"Great white shark","wrong":["Octopus","Killer whale","Catfish"]},{"id":"39397a83f44f","q":"What is radiation measured in?","correct":"Gray","wrong":["Watt","Decibel","Kelvin"]},{"id":"3869870dafae","q":"The human heart has how many chambers?","correct":"4","wrong":["2","6","3"]},{"id":"0ac9b9f6187a","q":"Which moon is the only satellite in our solar system to possess a dense atmosphere?","correct":"Titan","wrong":["Europa","Miranda","Callisto"]},{"id":"1e0a01a78354","q":"Down Syndrome is usually caused by an extra copy of which chromosome?","correct":"21","wrong":["23","15","24"]},{"id":"2375f79af6f0","q":"What is the first element on the periodic table?","correct":"Hydrogen","wrong":["Helium","Oxygen","Lithium"]},{"id":"d8f2b2f7bdd5","q":"Which of the following elements is typically used in the doping of the semiconductor silicon?","correct":"Boron","wrong":["Oxygen","Carbon","Iron"]},{"id":"446f58256a29","q":"What is the scientific term for 'taste'?","correct":"Gustatory Perception","wrong":["Olfaction","Somatosensation","Auditory Perception"]},{"id":"0b67f1172dc1","q":"What is the atomic number of the element Strontium?","correct":"38","wrong":["73","47","11"]},{"id":"1f6c3d5ad408","q":"What was the first living creature in space?","correct":"Fruit Flies","wrong":["Monkey","Dog","Mouse"]},{"id":"ebc86aec3d83","q":"What is the common name of the chemical compound \"dihydrogen monoxide\"?","correct":"Water","wrong":["Methane","Ammonia","Laughing Gas"]},{"id":"cb4c98e91764","q":"What does the letter 'S' stand for in 'NASA'?","correct":"Space","wrong":["Science","Society","Star"]},{"id":"522849c703a7","q":"How long is a light-year?","correct":"9.461 Trillion Kilometres","wrong":["1 AU","105.40 Earth-years","501.2 Million Miles"]},{"id":"20a747172c0b","q":"All of the following human genetic haplogroup names are shared between Y-chromosome and mitochondrial DNA haplogroups EXCEPT:","correct":"Haplogroup U","wrong":["Haplogroup L","Haplogroup T","Haplogroup J"]},{"id":"4be33db6620f","q":"How many chromosomes are in your body cells?","correct":"23","wrong":["21","22","24"]},{"id":"849e285341fb","q":"Where did the dog breed \"Chihuahua\" originate?","correct":"Mexico","wrong":["France","Spain","Russia"]},{"id":"7197119a813b","q":"Which of these choices is not one of the phases of mitosis?","correct":"Diplophase","wrong":["Metaphase","Anaphase","Telophase"]},{"id":"b433c90d6621","q":"Which of these is a stop codon in DNA?","correct":"TAA","wrong":["ACT","ACA","GTA"]},{"id":"ed359772aa4d","q":"Which of these is used to show that Earth spins on an axis?","correct":"Foucault Pendulum","wrong":["Polaris","Sundial","Tectonic Plates"]},{"id":"a8bd1993a2e6","q":"The word \"science\" stems from the word \"scire\" meaning what?","correct":"To know","wrong":["To measure","To live","To count"]},{"id":"61a72e93fc89","q":"What causes the sound of a heartbeat?","correct":"Closure of the heart valves","wrong":["Contraction of the heart chambers","Blood exiting the heart","Relaxation of the heart chambers"]},{"id":"1c5102b1fc2a","q":"Which of these elements on the Periodic Table is a Noble Gas?","correct":"Neon","wrong":["Potassium","Iodine","Colbalt"]},{"id":"9a06c2583792","q":"In physics, conservation of energy and conservation of momentum are both consequences of which of the following?","correct":"Noether's Theorem","wrong":["Bell's Theorem","Wick's Theorem","Carnot's Theorem"]},{"id":"5babe2b55a9c","q":"What is the primary addictive substance found in tobacco?","correct":"Nicotine","wrong":["Cathinone","Ephedrine","Glaucine"]},{"id":"ad69195de97a","q":"The element involved in making human blood red is which of the following?","correct":"Iron","wrong":["Copper","Iridium","Cobalt"]},{"id":"4d56bf5d7eda","q":"About how old is Earth?","correct":"4.5 Billion Years","wrong":["3.5 Billion Years","2.5 Billion Years","5.5 Billion Years"]},{"id":"30eecf95737e","q":"Which of the following is a major muscle of the back?","correct":"Trapezius","wrong":["Trapezium","Trapezoid","Triquetrum"]},{"id":"656a865673da","q":"The medical term for the belly button is which of the following?","correct":"Umbilicus","wrong":["Nevus","Nares","Paxillus"]},{"id":"9ee6465c5270","q":"In Chemistry, how many isomers does Butanol (C4H9OH) have?","correct":"4","wrong":["3","5","6"]},{"id":"9713bb83dc02","q":"At what depth should you make a decompression stop, or safety stop, on a typical scuba dive?","correct":"15 Feet / 5 Meters","wrong":["25 Feet / 7.5 Meters","50 Feet / 15 Meters","75 Feet / 23 Meters"]},{"id":"c61a3af82022","q":"Which chemical element was originally known as Alabamine?","correct":"Astatine","wrong":["Selenium","Antimony","Molybdenum"]},{"id":"70f1df14ead9","q":"Where did the Great Storm of 1987 make landfall at, first?","correct":"Cornwall","wrong":["Surrey","Wales","The Midlands"]},{"id":"0e34a94b93fe","q":"What is the atomic number of Uranium","correct":"92","wrong":["235","17","167"]},{"id":"6a622ccec049","q":"What mineral has the lowest number on the Mohs scale?","correct":"Talc","wrong":["Quartz","Diamond","Gypsum"]},{"id":"723a5c40c92a","q":"Stars consist mainly of hydrogen and which other gas?","correct":"Helium","wrong":["Oxygen","Argon","Nitrogen"]},{"id":"632629679b38","q":"At what temperature does water boil?","correct":"212&deg;F","wrong":["200&deg;F","181&deg;F","178&deg;F"]},{"id":"f46745833120","q":"What is the area of a circle with a diameter of 20 inches if &pi;= 3.1415?","correct":"314.15 Inches","wrong":["380.1215 Inches","3141.5 Inches","1256.6 Inches"]},{"id":"8f3dccd01bc6","q":"In Roman Numerals, what does XL equate to?","correct":"40","wrong":["60","15","90"]},{"id":"e2a78a0b38f0","q":"What is the approximate value of mathematical constant e?","correct":"2.72","wrong":["3.14","1.62","1.41"]},{"id":"87fe125ffd4f","q":"What is the derivative of sin(x)","correct":"cos(x)","wrong":["csc(x)","-cos(x)","-sin(x)"]},{"id":"8f9bc2bad9bf","q":"What is the mathematician Euler's first name?","correct":"Leonhard","wrong":["Lionel","Andrin","Ajan"]},{"id":"48a6d68b1f5d","q":"What is the correct order of operations for solving equations?","correct":"Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication, Division, Addition, Subtraction","wrong":["Addition, Multiplication, Division, Subtraction, Addition, Parentheses","Parentheses, Exponents, Addition, Substraction, Multiplication, Division","The order in which the operations are written."]},{"id":"0cfd71afbae3","q":"What comes after a Million, a Billion, and a Trillion?","correct":"Quadrillion","wrong":["Sextillion","Quintillion","Septillion"]},{"id":"3e512c4c22ce","q":"In a normal distribution, 95% of the data lies within how many standard deviations of the mean?","correct":"2","wrong":["1","3","4"]},{"id":"d93e2d6dfd5e","q":"A mathematical constant, known as \"The Golden Ratio\", is most commonly represented by which greek letter?","correct":"&Phi; (phi)","wrong":["&pi; (pi)","&Psi; (psi)","&Tau; (tau)"]},{"id":"70c55bef62f5","q":"Which of the following is not one of the seven Millennium Prize Problems?","correct":"Naviér conjecture","wrong":["Birch and Swinnerton-Dyer Conjecture","Riemann hypothesis","Poincaré conjecture"]},{"id":"5efec1dc400e","q":"What Greek letter is used to signify summation?","correct":"Sigma","wrong":["Delta","Alpha","Omega"]},{"id":"1637318734e1","q":"To the nearest whole number, how many radians are in a whole circle?","correct":"6","wrong":["3","4","5"]},{"id":"77f53a314850","q":"How many books are in Euclid's Elements of Geometry?","correct":"13","wrong":["8","10","17"]},{"id":"a1acc31e2ca8","q":"Which greek mathematician ran through the streets of Syracuse naked while shouting \"Eureka\" after discovering the principle of displacement?","correct":"Archimedes","wrong":["Euclid","Homer","Eratosthenes"]},{"id":"349f46235a27","q":"Which of these probability distributions is NOT discrete?","correct":"Normal","wrong":["Binomial","Poisson","Hyper-geometric"]},{"id":"3f4186cdd012","q":"Which of the following mathematicians made major contributions to game theory?","correct":"John Von Neumann","wrong":["Carl Friedrich Gauss","Leonhard Euler","Stefan Banach"]},{"id":"0728ce1f2710","q":"The decimal number 31 in hexadecimal would be what?","correct":"1F","wrong":["3D","2E","1B"]},{"id":"7d28997e6bd6","q":"How many zeptometres are inside one femtometre?","correct":"1,000,000","wrong":["10","1,000,000,000","1000"]},{"id":"8076457c9c45","q":"The French mathematician &Eacute;variste Galois is primarily known for his work in which?","correct":"Galois Theory","wrong":["Galois' Continued Fractions","Galois' Method for PDE's","Abelian Integration"]},{"id":"67c249b453bd","q":"What is the Roman numeral for 500?","correct":"D","wrong":["L","C","X"]},{"id":"bfc538af2e4d","q":"What prime number comes next after 19?","correct":"23","wrong":["25","21","27"]},{"id":"6ce4c12f96c6","q":"How many sides does a trapezium have?","correct":"4","wrong":["3","5","6"]},{"id":"d36be0c6b3fd","q":"What is the equation for the area of a sphere?","correct":"(4/3)&pi;r^3","wrong":["4&pi;r^2","(1/3)&pi;hr^2","&pi;r^4"]},{"id":"a32f68f7924e","q":"Which mathematician refused the Fields Medal?","correct":"Grigori Perelman","wrong":["Andrew Wiles","Terence Tao","Edward Witten"]},{"id":"cbd1fcc6c232","q":"The notion of a \"set that contains all sets which do not contain themselves\" is a paradoxical idea attributed to which English philosopher?","correct":"Bertrand Russel","wrong":["Francis Bacon","John Locke","Alfred North Whitehead"]},{"id":"b5a935f4ba34","q":"At what temperature does temp in &deg;C equal temp in &deg;F?","correct":"-40","wrong":["+40","0","+100"]},{"id":"e42460bd0fef","q":"What is the only Millennium Prize Problem that has been solved so far?","correct":"Poincaré conjecture","wrong":["P vs. NP problem","Riemann Hypothesis","Fermat's conjecture"]},{"id":"6656788a0b38","q":"In the complex plane, multiplying a given function by i rotates it anti-clockwise by how many degrees?","correct":"90","wrong":["180","270","0"]},{"id":"24f609e40475","q":"What type of angle is greater than 90&deg;?","correct":"Obtuse","wrong":["Acute","Right","Straight"]},{"id":"7152b2b08b7a","q":"What numbers are in the 5th row of Pascal's Triangle?","correct":"1 4 6 4 1","wrong":["1 3 3 1","1 5 10 10 5 1","1 6 15 20 15 6 1"]},{"id":"ddd6f0445700","q":"What is the fourth digit of &pi;?","correct":"1","wrong":["2","3","4"]},{"id":"e0127e7f0bc6","q":"How many square faces does a cube have?","correct":"6","wrong":["4","8","10"]},{"id":"c11831910567","q":"How many sides does a pentagon have?","correct":"5","wrong":["9","6","4"]},{"id":"6da81b006450","q":"How many sides does a heptagon have?","correct":"7","wrong":["5","4","9"]},{"id":"2e80d80b3c9e","q":"What are the first 6 digits of the number \"Pi\"?","correct":"3.14159","wrong":["3.14169","3.12423","3.25812"]},{"id":"5625af37fd4f","q":"What is a polygon with eight sides called?","correct":"Octagon","wrong":["Hexagon","Nanagon","Heptagon"]},{"id":"146101720782","q":"Integration is the reverse of what mathematical operation?","correct":"Derivation","wrong":["Division","Standard Deviation","Multiplication"]},{"id":"16cb72be6fb0","q":"In the hexadecimal system, what number comes after 9?","correct":"The Letter A","wrong":["10","The Number 0","16"]},{"id":"5e6b31f890ce","q":"Which of these numbers is closest to the total number of possible states for an army standard Enigma Machine?","correct":"1.58 x 10^20","wrong":["1.58 x 10^22","1.58 x  10^18","1.58 x 10^24"]},{"id":"c3fd75b2b640","q":"How many degrees make a full circle?","correct":"360","wrong":["180","90","720"]},{"id":"07492e84479d","q":"What is the first Mersenne prime exponent over 1000?","correct":"1279","wrong":["2203","1009","1069"]},{"id":"d72312143d85","q":"What's the square root of 49?","correct":"7","wrong":["4","12","9"]},{"id":"f0aa06f1d646","q":"What type of function is x&sup2;+2x+1?","correct":"Quadratic","wrong":["Rational","Linear","Exponential"]},{"id":"61b59473762f","q":"Which two men are credited with independently discovering differential calculus?","correct":"Newton and Leibnitz","wrong":["Plato and Aristotle","Asiimov and Rutherford","Dvorak and Smith"]},{"id":"fdc90fc07650","q":"What is the smallest number that can be expressed as the sum of two positive cubes in two different ways?","correct":"1729","wrong":["91","561","4104"]},{"id":"530df654d11d","q":"What is the derivative of Acceleration with respect to time?","correct":"Jerk","wrong":["Shift","Bump","Slide"]},{"id":"c737def69b85","q":"How many Millibars (mbar) to 1 Inch of Mercury (inHg)","correct":"33.9","wrong":["30.0","27.4","10.6"]},{"id":"966ef2d90735","q":"How many zeros are there in a googol?","correct":"100","wrong":["10","1,000","1,000,000"]},{"id":"3870096bbeda","q":"What is the alphanumeric representation of the imaginary number?","correct":"i","wrong":["e","n","x"]}],"tech":[{"id":"2ba3170aefb7","q":"Australia, Japan, and Southeast Asia are in which ITU Region?","correct":"Region 3","wrong":["Region 1","Region 2","Region 4"]},{"id":"8dc17bcaa376","q":"The programming language 'Swift' was created to replace what other programming language?","correct":"Objective-C","wrong":["C#","Ruby","C++"]},{"id":"9b05a6a71b3e","q":"Which coding language was the #1 programming language in terms of usage on GitHub in 2015?","correct":"JavaScript","wrong":["C#","Python","PHP"]},{"id":"0acd223bee84","q":"The Electron computer was released in Britain during 1983 for the home computing market, by which company?","correct":"Acorn Computers","wrong":["Sinclair Research","Amstrad PLC","Commodore Business Machines"]},{"id":"5989dce31390","q":"Linus Torvalds created which of these?","correct":"Linux","wrong":["Microsoft Windows","Python","Wikipedia"]},{"id":"b38caf523459","q":"How many bits are commonly in a single byte?","correct":"Eight bits","wrong":["Six bits","Twelve bits","Fifteen bits"]},{"id":"ccb0fb7d8c71","q":"Which company was established on April 1st, 1976 by Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak and Ronald Wayne?","correct":"Apple","wrong":["Microsoft","Atari","Commodore"]},{"id":"40c49f40bc3c","q":"Which computer language would you associate Django framework with?","correct":"Python","wrong":["C#","C++","Java"]},{"id":"dd5dfdf9c9c5","q":"What does the acronym CDN stand for in terms of networking?","correct":"Content Delivery Network","wrong":["Content Distribution Network","Computational Data Network","Compressed Data Network"]},{"id":"9afbe068e092","q":"The Windows OS was delevoped by which company?","correct":"Microsoft","wrong":["Apple","Nokia","IBM"]},{"id":"3e54b5f86a1a","q":"Released in 2001, the first edition of Apple's Mac OS X operating system (version 10.0) was given what animal code name?","correct":"Cheetah","wrong":["Puma","Tiger","Leopard"]},{"id":"2406fe111ab4","q":"Approximately how many Apple I personal computers were created?","correct":"200","wrong":["100","500","1000"]},{"id":"7acfd3304df0","q":"Which of these was the name of a bug found in April 2014 in the publicly available OpenSSL cryptography library?","correct":"Heartbleed","wrong":["Shellshock","Corrupted Blood","Shellscript"]},{"id":"bbd6ecc1be53","q":"The Harvard architecture for micro-controllers added which additional bus?","correct":"Instruction","wrong":["Address","Data","Control"]},{"id":"5efa52ea2935","q":"This mobile OS held the largest market share in 2012.","correct":"iOS","wrong":["Android","BlackBerry","Symbian"]},{"id":"cc36707c8e7d","q":"How many bytes are in a single Kibibyte?","correct":"1024","wrong":["2400","1000","1240"]},{"id":"332d5db3c596","q":"What is the most preferred image format used for logos in the Wikimedia database?","correct":".svg","wrong":[".png",".jpeg",".gif"]},{"id":"7309ffb1a9bb","q":"On which day did the World Wide Web go online?","correct":"December 20, 1990","wrong":["December 17, 1996","November 12, 1990","November 24, 1995"]},{"id":"41e4f381b0ca","q":"When did the online streaming service \"Mixer\" launch?","correct":"2016","wrong":["2013","2009","2011"]},{"id":"c4155489cbb2","q":"What did the name of the Tor Anonymity Network orignially stand for?","correct":"The Onion Router","wrong":["The Only Router","The Orange Router","The Ominous Router"]},{"id":"fcf4e1349dfd","q":"Lenovo acquired IBM's personal computer division, including the ThinkPad line of laptops and tablets, in what year?","correct":"2005","wrong":["1999","2002","2008"]},{"id":"4334068cc6e8","q":".at is the top-level domain for what country?","correct":"Austria","wrong":["Argentina","Australia","Angola"]},{"id":"7affa842dcb7","q":"What was the name of the image that features as the default background wallpaper for Windows XP?","correct":"Bliss","wrong":["Azul","Red moon desert","Tulips"]},{"id":"5ccbee347d75","q":"What kind of memory is used on memory cache?","correct":"SRAM","wrong":["DRAM","ROM","Flash"]},{"id":"7d0964f36909","q":"Moore's law originally stated that the number of transistors on a microprocessor chip would double every...","correct":"Year","wrong":["Four Years","Two Years","Eight Years"]},{"id":"cf991bfdd15b","q":"What does the computer software acronym JVM stand for?","correct":"Java Virtual Machine","wrong":["Java Vendor Machine","Java Visual Machine","Just Virtual Machine"]},{"id":"37b1f28100d6","q":"In computing, what does LAN stand for?","correct":"Local Area Network","wrong":["Long Antenna Node","Light Access Node","Land Address Navigation"]},{"id":"6bafaee378e3","q":"The numbering system with a radix of 16 is more commonly referred to as","correct":"Hexidecimal","wrong":["Binary","Duodecimal","Octal"]},{"id":"dfec1ad45649","q":"How many kilobytes in one gigabyte (in decimal)?","correct":"1000000","wrong":["1024","1000","1048576"]},{"id":"f8ed757bedb8","q":".rs is the top-level domain for what country?","correct":"Serbia","wrong":["Romania","Russia","Rwanda"]},{"id":"36f953d6fe6c","q":"The acronym \"RIP\" stands for which of these?","correct":"Routing Information Protocol","wrong":["Runtime Instance Processes","Regular Interval Processes","Routine Inspection Protocol"]},{"id":"a053540b2dc1","q":"What programming language was GitHub written in?","correct":"Ruby","wrong":["JavaScript","Python","Lua"]},{"id":"a9a77264f455","q":"The internet domain .fm is the country-code top-level domain for which Pacific Ocean island nation?","correct":"Micronesia","wrong":["Fiji","Tuvalu","Marshall Islands"]},{"id":"cbe709383555","q":"Which one of these is not an official development name for a Ubuntu release?","correct":"Mystic Mansion","wrong":["Trusty Tahr","Utopic Unicorn","Wily Werewolf"]},{"id":"ae367cae755b","q":"In programming, what do you call functions with the same name but different implementations?","correct":"Overloading","wrong":["Overriding","Abstracting","Inheriting"]},{"id":"ed67b4549e73","q":"In computing, how many bits are in a nibble?","correct":"4","wrong":["16","32","2"]},{"id":"3c6ba027f67b","q":"On which computer hardware device is the BIOS chip located?","correct":"Motherboard","wrong":["Hard Disk Drive","Central Processing Unit","Graphics Processing Unit"]},{"id":"31972cb5ecd3","q":"Which of the following is NOT a computer science algorithm?","correct":"Float Sort","wrong":["Bubble Sort","Merge Sort","Quick Sort"]},{"id":"a572a00ed1c1","q":"What language does Node.js use?","correct":"JavaScript","wrong":["Java","Java Source","Joomla Source Code"]},{"id":"6ffb5eb87ed2","q":"What does GHz stand for?","correct":"Gigahertz","wrong":["Gigahotz","Gigahetz","Gigahatz"]},{"id":"6bf1ef092be3","q":"Which of the following physical typologies are used with Ethernet Networks?","correct":"Star","wrong":["Ring","Mesh","Hex"]},{"id":"37951531dc86","q":"The name of technology company HP stands for what?","correct":"Hewlett-Packard","wrong":["Howard Packmann","Husker-Pollosk","Hellman-Pohl"]},{"id":"178b15c2786b","q":"What is the name given to layer 4 of the Open Systems Interconnection (ISO) model?","correct":"Transport","wrong":["Session","Data link","Network"]},{"id":"8609df2ed6c7","q":"Color model CMYK stands for?","correct":"Cyan, Magenta, Yellow, and Black","wrong":["Cream, Maroon, Yellow, and Black","Cyan, Magenta, Yellow, and Khaki","Cream, Maroon, Yellow, and Khaki"]},{"id":"ab8a1f59ca51","q":"On Twitter, what was the original character limit for a Tweet?","correct":"140","wrong":["120","160","100"]},{"id":"3d57ca154c67","q":"What does the 'S' in the RSA encryption algorithm stand for?","correct":"Shamir","wrong":["Secure","Schottky","Stable"]},{"id":"a83136c14403","q":"What does LTS stand for in the software market?","correct":"Long Term Support","wrong":["Long Taco Service","Ludicrous Transfer Speed","Ludicrous Turbo Speed"]},{"id":"679fca2f8f8b","q":"Which RAID array type is associated with data mirroring?","correct":"RAID 1","wrong":["RAID 0","RAID 10","RAID 5"]},{"id":"91ad2b17c629","q":"What does SSD stand for?","correct":"Solid State Drive","wrong":["Solution Source Disk","Solid State Disk","Source Solution Drive"]},{"id":"878e980bbe37","q":"What port does HTTP run on?","correct":"80","wrong":["53","443","23"]},{"id":"17b00cd33611","q":"All of the following programs are classified as raster graphics editors EXCEPT:","correct":"Inkscape","wrong":["Paint.NET","GIMP","Adobe Photoshop"]},{"id":"0e50fee7451d","q":"Which kind of algorithm is Ron Rivest not famous for creating?","correct":"Secret sharing scheme","wrong":["Hashing algorithm","Asymmetric encryption","Stream cipher"]},{"id":"e627f46a566d","q":"Which of these is the name for the failed key escrow device introduced by the National Security Agency in 1993?","correct":"Clipper Chip","wrong":["Enigma Machine","Skipjack","Nautilus"]},{"id":"975adca3e834","q":"What does the International System of Quantities refer 1024 bytes as?","correct":"Kibibyte","wrong":["Kylobyte","Kilobyte","Kelobyte"]},{"id":"2fcf15d9690e","q":"What is the number of keys on a standard Windows Keyboard?","correct":"104","wrong":["64","94","76"]},{"id":"a61e53108caf","q":"What is the main CPU is the Sega Mega Drive / Sega Genesis?","correct":"Motorola 68000","wrong":["Zilog Z80","Yamaha YM2612","Intel 8088"]},{"id":"eeb42cb0c7a1","q":"Which of the following is a personal computer made by the Japanese company Fujitsu?","correct":"FM-7","wrong":["PC-9801","Xmillennium","MSX"]},{"id":"85d8b618a2c5","q":"What is the maximum value of a 32-bit signed binary integer?","correct":"2,147,483,647","wrong":["255","2048","9,223,372,036,854,775,807"]},{"id":"a84ddee58002","q":"What is the codename of the eighth generation Intel Core micro-architecture launched in October 2017?","correct":"Coffee Lake","wrong":["Sandy Bridge","Skylake","Broadwell"]},{"id":"ec018b5ff86f","q":"What was the first Android version specifically optimized for tablets?","correct":"Honeycomb","wrong":["Eclair","Froyo","Marshmellow"]},{"id":"2c3a8ca8931b","q":"What does the term GPU stand for?","correct":"Graphics Processing Unit","wrong":["Gaming Processor Unit","Graphite Producing Unit","Graphical Proprietary Unit"]},{"id":"c97e33217385","q":"Which computer hardware device provides an interface for all other connected devices to communicate?","correct":"Motherboard","wrong":["Central Processing Unit","Hard Disk Drive","Random Access Memory"]},{"id":"72840a187479","q":"Which of these names was an actual codename for a cancelled Microsoft project?","correct":"Neptune","wrong":["Enceladus","Pollux","Saturn"]},{"id":"46b41ca8f108","q":"According to DeMorgan's Theorem, the Boolean expression (AB)' is equivalent to:","correct":"A' + B'","wrong":["A'B + B'A","A'B'","AB' + AB"]},{"id":"581fb9459f71","q":"Which of these is not a key value of Agile software development?","correct":"Comprehensive documentation","wrong":["Individuals and interactions","Customer collaboration","Responding to change"]},{"id":"6381696ef8c5","q":"What is the name of Layer 7 of the OSI model?","correct":"Application","wrong":["Session","Network","Present"]},{"id":"d1702569dd8b","q":"What does CPU stand for?","correct":"Central Processing Unit","wrong":["Central Process Unit","Computer Personal Unit","Central Processor Unit"]},{"id":"2a01159773ae","q":"The C programming language was created by this A