","60","25"]},{"id":"27001a8417de","q":"Which of the following is the oldest of these computers by release date?","correct":"TRS-80","wrong":["Commodore 64","ZX Spectrum","Apple 3"]},{"id":"dfd47304c518","q":"Laserjet and inkjet printers are both examples of what type of printer?","correct":"Non-impact printer","wrong":["Impact printer","Daisywheel printer","Dot matrix printer"]},{"id":"c630b1ae244f","q":"When was the programming language \"C#\" released?","correct":"2000","wrong":["1998","1999","2001"]},{"id":"f01e09183b7f","q":"What does the DOS in Microsoft's first operating system \"MS-DOS\" stand for?","correct":"Disk Operating System","wrong":["Dumb Operating System","Driver Oriented System","Diskless Operating System"]},{"id":"3bd188203241","q":"What was the first company to use the term \"Golden Master\"?","correct":"Apple","wrong":["IBM","Microsoft","Google"]},{"id":"767a714822f1","q":"Whistler was the codename of this Microsoft Operating System.","correct":"Windows XP","wrong":["Windows 2000","Windows 7","Windows 95"]},{"id":"f8dd1d507a3c","q":"Which of the following languages is used as a scripting language in the Unity 3D game engine?","correct":"C#","wrong":["Java","C++","Objective-C"]},{"id":"4669720bc90c","q":"Which of these people was NOT a founder of Apple Inc?","correct":"Jonathan Ive","wrong":["Steve Jobs","Ronald Wayne","Steve Wozniak"]},{"id":"dae6108d2630","q":"In CSS, which of these values CANNOT be used with the \"position\" property?","correct":"center","wrong":["static","absolute","relative"]},{"id":"930bea18fbe3","q":"Which internet company began life as an online bookstore called 'Cadabra'?","correct":"Amazon","wrong":["eBay","Overstock","Shopify"]},{"id":"b456c6bb4d79","q":"What does the term USB stand for?","correct":"Universal Serial Bus","wrong":["Universal Simtex Blot","Unified Signal Bus","Unityped Semtex Backer"]},{"id":"a9cf5e61fe58","q":"What was the name of the first Bulgarian personal computer?","correct":"IMKO-1","wrong":["Pravetz 82","Pravetz 8D","IZOT 1030"]},{"id":"751047e0665a","q":"What does \"LCD\" stand for?","correct":"Liquid Crystal Display","wrong":["Language Control Design","Last Common Difference","Long Continuous Design"]},{"id":"9b2374965a37","q":"What is the commonly used keyboard shortcut for the 'Copy' function on Windows OS?","correct":"Ctrl + C","wrong":["Ctrl + X","Alt + C","Alt + X"]},{"id":"6aed16b7deed","q":"CMOS is tech used for constructing integrated circuits. What does CMOS stand for?","correct":"Complementary metal–oxide–semiconductor","wrong":["Complementary magnetic-ohms-semiconductor","Computer-made operating system","Computer-made oscillating static"]},{"id":"92bbfe73bbf8","q":"Nvidia's headquarters are based in which Silicon Valley city?","correct":"Santa Clara","wrong":["Palo Alto","Cupertino","Mountain View"]},{"id":"8f56f90da444","q":"In computing, what does MIDI stand for?","correct":"Musical Instrument Digital Interface","wrong":["Musical Interface of Digital Instruments","Modular Interface of Digital Instruments","Musical Instrument Data Interface"]},{"id":"6d930f9230d1","q":"Which data structure does FILO apply to?","correct":"Stack","wrong":["Queue","Heap","Tree"]},{"id":"e901a1bf0d8d","q":"What type of sound chip does the Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) have?","correct":"ADPCM Sampler","wrong":["FM Synthesizer","Programmable Sound Generator (PSG)","PCM Sampler"]},{"id":"ceb6023d9603","q":"What five letter word is the motto of the IBM Computer company?","correct":"Think","wrong":["Click","Logic","Pixel"]},{"id":"25d74660434a","q":"In programming, the ternary operator is mostly defined with what symbol(s)?","correct":"?:","wrong":["??","if then","?"]}],"entertainment":[{"id":"e211f57f0dbc","q":"In order to cut costs, what were most of the extras of Mad Max (1979) paid with?","correct":"Beer","wrong":["Fast food","Food stamps","They weren't paid"]},{"id":"2284a04041ae","q":"In the movie Gremlins, after what time of day should you not feed Mogwai?","correct":"Midnight","wrong":["Evening","Morning","Afternoon"]},{"id":"01b0fd4545e5","q":"What name did Tom Hanks give to his volleyball companion in the film `Cast Away`?","correct":"Wilson","wrong":["Friday","Jones","Billy"]},{"id":"474aa3836ce3","q":"The Queen song `A Kind Of Magic` is featured in which 1986 film?","correct":"Highlander","wrong":["Flash Gordon","Labyrinth","Howard the Duck"]},{"id":"d7e685250917","q":"Which of these actors does NOT appear in the 1998 movie \"Saving Private Ryan\"?","correct":"Ralph Fiennes","wrong":["Tom Hanks","Vin Diesel","Matt Damon"]},{"id":"5cda5b0be3d5","q":"What movie starring Bruce Willis contains the line \"I see dead people\"?","correct":"The Sixth Sense","wrong":["The Fifth Element","Die Hard","Armageddon"]},{"id":"0c8f64483285","q":"\"The first rule is: you don't talk about it\" is a reference to which movie?","correct":"Fight Club","wrong":["The Island","Unthinkable","American Pie"]},{"id":"6243576a4dd5","q":"Before getting the shotgun, what did the titular hobo in 'Hobo with a Shotgun' want to purchase?","correct":"a lawnmower","wrong":["a revolver","a guitar","a suit"]},{"id":"4627f6679808","q":"Who wrote and directed the 1986 film 'Platoon'?","correct":"Oliver Stone","wrong":["Francis Ford Coppola","Stanley Kubrick","Michael Cimino"]},{"id":"9b3f0ef2e8ec","q":"What type of cheese, loved by Wallace and Gromit, had it's sale prices rise after their successful short films?","correct":"Wensleydale","wrong":["Cheddar","Moon Cheese","Edam"]},{"id":"6335aa2c9da9","q":"In Big Hero 6, what were Baymax's motions modeled after?","correct":"Baby penguins","wrong":["Baby monkeys","Baby ostriches","Baby bears"]},{"id":"3e67facc1533","q":"What American actor directed and co-starred alongside Emily Blunt in 2018's horror film \"A Quiet Place\"?","correct":"John Krasinski","wrong":["Keanu Reeves","Willem Dafoe","Josh Brolin"]},{"id":"ab7e0ad651e0","q":"What is the make and model of the tour vehicles in \"Jurassic Park\" 