ternational championships?","correct":"Santa Clara Vanguard","wrong":["Blue Devils","The Academy","The Bluecoats"]},{"id":"5ec2dad5b98a","q":"What is the name of Metallica's debut album, released in 1983?","correct":"Kill 'Em All","wrong":["...And Justice for All","Master of Puppets","Countdown to Extinction"]},{"id":"348860756a29","q":"What album did The Lumineers release in 2016?","correct":"Cleopatra","wrong":["Winter","The Lumineers","Tracks From The Attic"]},{"id":"44307131fc48","q":"What year did Dire Straits's Song \"Money for Nothing\" release?","correct":"1985","wrong":["1973","1980","1991"]},{"id":"c0ea7ca2d42c","q":"What genre of EDM is the Dutch DJ, musician, and remixer Armin van Buuren most well-known for?","correct":"Trance","wrong":["House","Drum and Bass","Dubstep"]},{"id":"088dc0d75c18","q":"La Fenice opera house is in which Italian city?","correct":"Venice","wrong":["Milan","Rome","Pompeii"]},{"id":"d10d88ef35ba","q":"Which musical group won the Brit Awards in 1985, with George Michael as a member?","correct":"Wham!","wrong":["Frankie Goes to Hollywood","U2","Culture Club"]},{"id":"90ebe8a0718e","q":"A classic 1976 song by Blue Oyster Cult features the advice “Don’t Fear The” what?","correct":"Reaper","wrong":["Dark","Silence","Clowns"]},{"id":"87eb29d12f2b","q":"The co-creator of Gorillaz, Damon Albarn, is also the lead singer of what band?","correct":"Blur","wrong":["Oasis","Radiohead","Queens of the Stone Age"]},{"id":"c6d4a007deaa","q":"Björk's \"Unison\" contains a sample of which Oval song?","correct":"Aero Deck","wrong":["Textuell","Panorama","Do While"]},{"id":"4b61ac14922e","q":"Which band released songs such as \"Electric Feel\", \"Kids\", and \"Time to Pretend\"?","correct":"MGMT","wrong":["Passion Pit","Phoenix","Franz Ferdinand"]},{"id":"a7f5021d1221","q":"Which singer was featured in Swedish producer Avicii's song \"Wake Me Up\"?","correct":"Aloe Blacc","wrong":["John Legend","CeeLo Green","Pharrell Williams"]},{"id":"6c81e830b17d","q":"Which Beatles album does NOT feature any of the band members on it's cover?","correct":"The Beatles (White Album)","wrong":["Rubber Soul","Abbey Road","Magical Mystery Tour"]},{"id":"33456b9b9569","q":"What collaborative album was released by Kanye West and Jay-Z in 2011?","correct":"Watch the Throne","wrong":["Distant Relatives","What a Time to be Alive","Unfinished Business"]},{"id":"6b8eb084a4c1","q":"What was The Velvet Underground's first album called?","correct":"The Velvet Underground & Nico","wrong":["Loaded","The Velvet Underground","White Light / White Heat"]},{"id":"00b6c31d29df","q":"Which country does the power metal band \"Sabaton\" originate from?","correct":"Sweden","wrong":["Germany","United States","Finland"]},{"id":"b930e3fd1b82","q":"Which famous 90's rap album is commonly referred to as \"The Bible of Hip Hop\"?","correct":"Illmatic","wrong":["The Low End Theory","The Chronic","Enter The Wu-Tang (36 Chambers)"]},{"id":"c3ce9041ceca","q":"What album did Bon Iver release in 2016?","correct":"22, A Million","wrong":["Bon Iver, Bon Iver","Blood Bank EP","For Emma, Forever Ago"]},{"id":"6b46c4cffa1c","q":"Who was the first Jazz Musician to win the Pulitzer Prize for Music","correct":"Wynton Marsalis","wrong":["Michael Brecker","Herbie Hancock","Joe Henderson"]},{"id":"e9221e82e28f","q":"What French artist/band is known for playing on the midi instrument \"Launchpad\"?","correct":"Madeon","wrong":["Daft Punk","Disclosure","David Guetta"]},{"id":"7c5428930bd1","q":"Who is the lead singer of The Lumineers?","correct":"Wesley Schultz","wrong":["Jeremiah Fraites","Jay Van Dyke","Neyla Pekarek"]},{"id":"8043631a3f8f","q":"In The Bangles' 'Manic Monday', what time is it already?","correct":"Six o'clock","wrong":["Five o'clock","Four o'clock","Seven o'clock"]},{"id":"f53e5537748c","q":"The heavy metal band Black Sabbath hail from which English city?","correct":"Birmingham","wrong":["Manchester","London","Newcastle-Upon-Tyne"]},{"id":"b3781ff9e8f7","q":"What animal is featured on the cover of English electronic music group The Prodigy's album, \"The Fat of the Land\"?","correct":"Crab","wrong":["Fox","Elephant","Tiger"]},{"id":"896e5513b791","q":"What was the name of singer Frank Ocean's second studio album, which was released on August 20, 2016?","correct":"Blonde","wrong":["Brunette","Black","Burgundy"]},{"id":"431245a4c14c","q":"Which country is singer Kyary Pamyu Pamyu from?","correct":"Japan","wrong":["South Korea","China","Vietnam"]},{"id":"d1f86e1478a0","q":"Who is the bassist of the British rock band Queen?","correct":"John Deacon","wrong":["John Major","John Barrowman","John Mayer"]},{"id":"1b221a6127b4","q":"How many studio albums have the heavy metal band, 'Metallica' released in the period between 1983 and 2016?","correct":"10","wrong":["7","9","12"]},{"id":"4753e66b3353","q":"Which rap group released the album \"Straight Outta Compton\"?","correct":"N.W.A","wrong":["Wu-Tang Clan","Run-D.M.C.","Beastie Boys"]},{"id":"8f3763f08a7c","q":"Which English guitarist has the nickname \"Slowhand\"?","correct":"Eric Clapton","wrong":["Mark Knopfler","Jeff Beck","Jimmy Page"]},{"id":"50836e9a91db","q":"When did Radiohead release their album \"OK Computer\"?","correct":"1997","wrong":["1995","2000","1993"]},{"id":"c3e6baa3870b","q":"African-American performer Sammy Davis Jr. was known for losing which part of his body in a car accident?","correct":"Left Eye","wrong":["Right Ear","Right Middle Finger","Nose"]},{"id":"53defe178e99","q":"Who was the original drummer for The Beatles?","correct":"Tommy Moore","wrong":["Ringo Starr","Stuart Sutcliffe","Pete Best"]},{"id":"8eb152482b6e","q":"Who was walking like an Egyptian in 1981?","correct":"The Bangles","wrong":["R.E.M.","The Ocean Blue","The Connells"]},{"id":"9f4911ea5c50","q":"What date is referenced in the 1971 song \"September\" by Earth, Wind & Fire?","correct":"21st of September","wrong":["26th of September","23rd of September","24th of September"]},{"id":"48f46