efore his decade-long hiatus?","correct":"Drukqs","wrong":["Windowlicker","Syro","Collected Ambient Works 85-92"]},{"id":"ded721091b12","q":"Which chain restaurant increased sales after it was mentioned in the 2016 Beyoncé song: \"Formation\"?","correct":"Red Lobster","wrong":["Outback Steakhouse","TGI Fridays","Applebee's"]},{"id":"2e571c73837e","q":"In August 1964, who introduced the Beatles to cannabis?","correct":"Bob Dylan","wrong":["Jim Morrison","Brian Epstein","Jerry Garcia"]},{"id":"547bf69f6ed7","q":"What was the first music video to be broadcast on MTV?","correct":"Video Killed the Radio Star","wrong":["Take On Me","Walk This Way","Hungry Like the Wolf"]},{"id":"7169f678466d","q":"In the  Rossini opera, what was the name of 'The Barber of Seville'?","correct":"Figaro","wrong":["Angelo","Fernando","Dave"]},{"id":"eca6356b1661","q":"What is the frontman's name of the metal band Megadeth?","correct":"Dave Mustaine","wrong":["Rob Halford","Vince Neil","James Hetfield"]},{"id":"7215742cfc24","q":"In music theory, how many notes are in a seventh chord?","correct":"4","wrong":["3","7","2"]},{"id":"e9f86080565b","q":"Which song made by MAN WITH A MISSION was used as the opening for the anime \"Log Horizon\"?","correct":"\"Database\"","wrong":["\"Dead End in Tokyo\"","\"Raise Your Flag\"","\"Out of Control\""]},{"id":"3c8ea3419812","q":"Which of these black metal acts was a solo project?","correct":"Burzum","wrong":["Darkthrone","Mayhem","Dissection"]},{"id":"39a490eff8e4","q":"What was the release date of the They Might Be Giants album, 'Mink Car?'","correct":"September 11th, 2001","wrong":["April 17th, 2003","November 4th, 1999","December 20th, 2002"]},{"id":"6a296691da43","q":"In the metal band Slipknot, there are 9 members, which member labelled themselves number 6?","correct":"Shawn Crahan (Clown)","wrong":["Sid Wilson","Cory Taylor","Mick Thomson"]},{"id":"d93b05668162","q":"On which Beatles album would you find the song 'Eleanor Rigby'?","correct":"Revolver","wrong":["Help!","Rubber Soul","Abbey Road"]},{"id":"0f6e6596d333","q":"The Who's eponymous line, \"Teenage Wasteland\", appears in which of their songs?","correct":"Baba O' Riley","wrong":["The Seeker","Won't Get Fooled Again","Pinball Wizard"]},{"id":"3b725891cf55","q":"Who is the lead singer of Pearl Jam?","correct":"Eddie Vedder","wrong":["Ozzy Osbourne","Stone Gossard","Kurt Cobain"]},{"id":"99fcaa28e5b2","q":"What are the first few words in the lyrics of A-Ha's 'Take On Me'?","correct":"We're talking away","wrong":["We're dreaming today","We're finding a way","We're blocking the way"]},{"id":"85356152f5c9","q":"In 2015, David Hasselhof released a single called...","correct":"True Survivor","wrong":["True Fighter","Real Kung-Fury","Real Warrior"]},{"id":"82edffa7a20d","q":"How many strings are there on a cello?","correct":"4","wrong":["5","6","8"]},{"id":"506e31aea0a3","q":"Which of the Beatles band members is barefoot on the front cover of the 'Abbey Road' album?","correct":"Paul McCartney","wrong":["Ringo Starr","George Harrison","John Lennon"]},{"id":"1ad88b67930f","q":"Which one of these Pink Floyd albums were also a movie?","correct":"The Wall","wrong":["The Dark Side of the Moon","Wish You Were Here","Animals"]},{"id":"37d37444cfcf","q":"Who is the lead singer of Green Day?","correct":"Billie Joe Armstrong","wrong":["Mike Dirnt","Sean Hughes","Tré Cool"]},{"id":"5a940a862a18","q":"Which member of the Wu-Tang Clan had only one verse in their debut album Enter the Wu-Tang (36 Chambers)?","correct":"Masta Killa","wrong":["Method Man","Inspectah Deck","GZA"]},{"id":"57ef6beda349","q":"Who was featured in the song \"Words\" by Feint?","correct":"Laura Brehm","wrong":["Anna Yvette","Danyka Nadeau","Veela"]},{"id":"d8b57247b7eb","q":"Who had a US and UK number 1 hit in 1962 with the instrumental, 'Telstar'?","correct":"The Tornados","wrong":["The Ventures","The Spotnicks","The Tremeloes"]},{"id":"da3c51697b98","q":"Who is the frontman of the band 30 Seconds to Mars?","correct":"Jared Leto","wrong":["Gerard Way","Matthew Bellamy","Mike Shinoda"]},{"id":"5e1fc6f1cf80","q":"Who had a 1981 hit with the song \"Japanese Boy\"?","correct":"Aneka","wrong":["Toyah","Sandra","Madonna"]},{"id":"97174d696e5a","q":"Who had hits in the 70s with the songs \"Lonely Boy\" and \"Never Let Her Slip Away\"?","correct":"Andrew Gold","wrong":["Elton John","Leo Sayer","Barry White"]},{"id":"8059eb9c13c3","q":"Who is the musical artist who released the hit song, \"Love Song,\" in 2007?","correct":"Sara Bareilles","wrong":["Taylor Swift","Katy Perry","Sarah Silverman"]},{"id":"2912a65b43ee","q":"Which 80s band is fronted by singer/guitarist Robert Smith?","correct":"The Cure","wrong":["The Smiths","Echo & the Bunnymen","New Order"]},{"id":"c83119d9277c","q":"What is the name of the second studio album released by American rapper Post Malone in 2018?","correct":"Beerbongs & Bentleys","wrong":["Takin' Shots","Rockstar","Better Now"]},{"id":"1b00f418f90a","q":"What is the British term for a 64th note?","correct":"Hemidemisemiquaver","wrong":["Semihemidemisemiquaver","Semiquaver","Demisemiquaver"]},{"id":"31f9126c45ea","q":"Which of the following rappers were NOT part of the hip-hop group Odd Future?","correct":"Vince Staples","wrong":["Tyler, the Creator","Frank Ocean","Mike G"]},{"id":"4a7be411bc12","q":"Who was \"Kung Fu Fighting\" in 1974?","correct":"Carl Douglas","wrong":["The Bee Gees","Heatwave","Kool & the Gang"]},{"id":"db880fa3bc00","q":"Which European capital city gives its name to a 1981 song by Ultravox?","correct":"Vienna","wrong":["Berlin","Paris","Brussels"]},{"id":"be0827944207","q":"Which Beatle led the way across the zebra crossing on the Abbey Road album cover?","correct":"John","wrong":["Paul","George","Ringo"]},{"id":"bfce0e6df967","q":"Which of these bands is the oldest?","correct":"Pink Floyd","wrong":["AC/DC","Metallica","Red Hot Chili Peppers"]},{"id":"769ed5ba08f8","q":"What is the first track on the Dave Matthews Band album \"Before These Crowded Streets\"?","correct":"Pantala Naga Pampa","wrong":["Stay (Wasting Time)","Rapunzel","Don't Drink The Water"]},{"id":"ff26ef91ac94","q":"A piccolo is a smaller version of what instrument?","correct":"Flute","wrong":["Trumpet","Harp","Violin"]},{"id":"b5e67dabb876","q":"Korean girl group TWICE is under which Entertainment Label?","correct":"JYP","wrong":["MBK","YG","Stone Music"]},{"id":"285448f2341c","q":"Who is the lead singer of the Smashing Pumpkins?","correct":"Billy Corgan","wrong":["Brett Scallions","Eddie Vedder","Chino Moreno"]},{"id":"c7a7674e32ef","q":"The song \"Old Town Road\" by American rapper Lil Nas X samples the song \"34 Ghosts IV\" by which band?","correct":"Nine Inch Nails","wrong":["Death Grips","Iron Maiden","Animal Collective"]},{"id":"37de2293d0eb","q":"What was the subject of the 2014 song \"CoCo\" by American rapper O. T. Genasis?","correct":"Cocaine","wrong":["Conan O'Brien","Cobalt(II) carbonate","Coconut cream pie"]},{"id":"be0600ec774a","q":"The 2016 song \"Starboy\" by Canadian singer The Weeknd features which prominent electronic artist?","correct":"Daft Punk","wrong":["deadmau5","Disclosure","DJ Shadow"]},{"id":"917241cdaefb","q":"The 'In the Flesh' tour was used in support of what Pink Floyd album?","correct":"Animals","wrong":["The Wall","Wish You Were Here","The Final Cut"]},{"id":"097fce42a261","q":"Which French duo had UK hits in 1998 with the songs 'Sexy Boy', 'Kelly Watch The Stars' & 'All I Need'?","correct":"Air","wrong":["Fire","Earth","Water"]},{"id":"5212eccf3dc0","q":"Which famous artist featured on Rowdy Rebel's 2015 song \"Computers\"?","correct":"Bobby Shmurda","wrong":["Lil Wayne","Will.I.AM","Kendrick Lamar"]},{"id":"f4deaf970cd0","q":"Which Canadian reggae musician had a 1993 hit with the song 'Informer'?","correct":"Snow","wrong":["Rain","Hail","Sleet"]},{"id":"66f6ec2cc260","q":"Which lyric is about Red Hot Chili Peppers frontman Anthony Kiedis?","correct":"\"A rainy Lithuanian / Is dancing as an Indian\"","wrong":["\"Fly away on, my zephyr / I feel it more than ever\"","\"And I liked the dimple in your chin / Your pale blue eyes\"","\"You used to be so warm and affectionate...but now you're quick to get into your regret\""]},{"id":"04d08572677d","q":"'The Safety Dance' was the biggest hit single for which Canadian act?","correct":"Men Without Hats","wrong":["Crash Test Dummies","The Tragically Hip","Broken Social Scene"]},{"id":"3cab5aff1fc6","q":"What song by Tina Turner is the theme for Mad Max Beyond Thunderdome?","correct":"We Don't Need Another Hero","wrong":["Let's Stay Together","What's Love Got To Do With It","I Don't Wanna Lose You"]},{"id":"c3c13fe12d05","q":"Ellie Goulding's earliest album was named?","correct":"Lights","wrong":["Halcyon","Bright Lights","Halcyon Days"]},{"id":"f42fa840af72","q":"Who is the lead singer of the band Coldplay?","correct":"Chris Martin","wrong":["Chris Isaak","Chris Wallace","Chris Connelly"]},{"id":"0f30a5cb66b0","q":"What is Justin Bieber's debut Album?","correct":"My World 2.0","wrong":["U Smile","Baby","Purpose"]},{"id":"5f6bc3d06914","q":"Grand Theft Autumn/Where Is Your Boy is a song by which band?","correct":"Fall Out Boy","wrong":["Panic! At The Disco","Paramore","Blink-182"]},{"id":"ad4e9fb5ced4","q":"Which of these songs by Skrillex features Fatman Scoop as a side artist?","correct":"Recess","wrong":["All is Fair in Love and Brostep","Rock N Roll (Will Take You to the Mountain)","Scary Monsters and Nice Sprites"]},{"id":"38402e4d13c7","q":"Which song is NOT by singer Tom Jones?","correct":"Never Gonna Give You Up","wrong":["It's Not Unusual","What's New Pussycat","Delilah"]},{"id":"777313e4e002","q":"Which of these songs is not on the \"untitled\" album by Led Zeppelin?","correct":"Celebration Day","wrong":["Stairway to Heaven","Black Dog","Rock and Roll"]},{"id":"fa01e6dc5412","q":"Ringo Starr of The Beatles mainly played what instrument?","correct":"Drums","wrong":["Bass","Guitar","Piano"]},{"i