erica?","correct":"Washington D.C","wrong":["Seattle","Albany","Los Angeles"]},{"id":"d56da307e5bd","q":"Which of the following Japanese islands is the biggest?","correct":"Honshu","wrong":["Hokkaido","Shikoku","Kyushu"]},{"id":"d075727ab71a","q":"Into which basin does the Jordan River flow into?","correct":"Dead Sea","wrong":["Aral Sea","Caspian Sea","Salton Sea"]},{"id":"0efa190fc61f","q":"Where is the area commonly known as the Bermuda Triangle?","correct":"North Atlantic Ocean, between Florida and Puerto Rico","wrong":["North Pacific Ocean, between Japan and the USA","In the Caribbean Sea","South Pacific Ocean, far off Chile"]},{"id":"b1a546eb2e68","q":"Greenland is a part of which kingdom?","correct":"Denmark","wrong":["Sweden","Norway","United Kingdom"]},{"id":"069767c1ccb8","q":"Which of these African countries list \"Spanish\" as an official language?","correct":"Equatorial Guinea","wrong":["Guinea","Cameroon","Angola"]},{"id":"1148ebd2a4f0","q":"Which one of these archipelagos are NOT a part of the United Kingdom?","correct":"The Channel Islands","wrong":["Orkney Islands","Isles of Scilly","Shetland Islands"]},{"id":"bbea255d8429","q":"Montreal is in which Canadian province?","correct":"Quebec","wrong":["Ontario","Nova Scotia","Alberta"]},{"id":"4b1fab16bd00","q":"What is the capital of Wisconsin, USA?","correct":"Madison","wrong":["Milwaukee","Wisconsin Dells","Green Bay"]},{"id":"6f295ff71433","q":"Which of these is NOT a city in Saudi Arabia?","correct":"Dubai","wrong":["Riyadh","Mecca","Medina"]},{"id":"e2b79afa5636","q":"What is the tallest mountain in Canada?","correct":"Mount Logan","wrong":["Mont Tremblant","Whistler Mountain","Blue Mountain"]},{"id":"af81c2f47c05","q":"How many countries share a land border with Russia? (Not including disputed territories)","correct":"14","wrong":["12","10","8"]},{"id":"4ff01e9f0bf0","q":"How many timezones does Russia have?","correct":"11","wrong":["6","24","16"]},{"id":"47b3e9a5e652","q":"The following Spanish provinces are located in the northern area of Spain except:","correct":"Murcia","wrong":["Asturias","Navarre","Le&oacute;n"]},{"id":"a6fde9897fbd","q":"Which of these is NOT an Australian state or territory?","correct":"Alberta","wrong":["New South Wales","Victoria","Queensland"]},{"id":"4178dfeb58c1","q":"Which of the following is not a megadiverse country - one that harbors a high number of the earth's endemic species?","correct":"Thailand","wrong":["Peru","Mexico","South Africa"]},{"id":"1165118ed01a","q":"What is the capital city of the U.S. state of Texas?","correct":"Austin","wrong":["Dallas","Houston","San Antonio"]},{"id":"0db533375df2","q":"What national museum will you find in Cooperstown, New York?","correct":"National Baseball Hall of Fame","wrong":["Metropolitan Museum of Art","National Toy Hall of Fame","Museum of Modern Art"]},{"id":"a060f647a209","q":"What is the capital of Finland?","correct":"Helsinki","wrong":["Jabraltar","Macedonia","Oslo"]},{"id":"0c06e5a6efcd","q":"Which area of Eastern Europe is famous for its association with vampires?","correct":"Transylvania","wrong":["Silesia","Macedonia","Slovakia"]},{"id":"d6b0aec5d532","q":"Which US state is nicknamed \"The Golden State\"?","correct":"California","wrong":["Florida","New Mexico","Alaska"]},{"id":"1b203c4317a8","q":"Which of the following landlocked countries is entirely contained within another country?","correct":"Lesotho","wrong":["Burkina Faso","Mongolia","Luxembourg"]},{"id":"0829d0915df2","q":"Which city is the capital of Switzerland?","correct":"Bern","wrong":["Zürich","Frankfurt","Wien"]},{"id":"990bccbce44d","q":"What is the name of the capital of Turkey?","correct":"Ankara","wrong":["Istanbul","Izmir","Bursa"]},{"id":"8feeed10cd72","q":"Which of these is NOT a city in India?","correct":"Islamabad","wrong":["Hyderabad","Ahmedabad","Ghaziabad"]},{"id":"76771d5ff0ae","q":"Which of these Mediterranian islands is under the sovereign rule of France?","correct":"Corsica","wrong":["Majorca","Sardinia","Malta"]},{"id":"f7e21d40aba4","q":"What is the capital of the State of Washington, United States?","correct":"Olympia","wrong":["Washington D.C.","Seattle","Yukon"]},{"id":"496775c041e9","q":"All of the following are classified as Finno-Ugric languages EXCEPT:","correct":"Samoyedic","wrong":["Hungarian","Finnish","Estonian"]},{"id":"0fb7517ef08e","q":"Which UK country features a dragon on their flag?","correct":"Wales","wrong":["England","North Ireland","Scotland"]},{"id":"89d1af658d1b","q":"The land mass of modern day Turkey is called what?","correct":"Anatolia","wrong":["Ismuth of Ottoma","Ottoma","Ismuth of Anatolia"]},{"id":"33183ed0da2c","q":"What is the official national language of Pakistan?","correct":"Urdu","wrong":["Indian","Punjabi","Pashto"]},{"id":"d8cb659de7af","q":"Which of these American cities has fewer than 1,000,000 people?","correct":"San Francisco, California","wrong":["Phoenix, Arizona","San Antonio, Texas","Philadelphia, Pennsylvania"]},{"id":"076b47cceb45","q":"Which country features a maple leaf on its flag?","correct":"Canada","wrong":["Mexico","Brazil","India"]},{"id":"504be8f97b97","q":"How many federal states does Germany have?","correct":"16","wrong":["13","32","25"]},{"id":"1c21715d2496","q":"Guyana is in which continent?","correct":"South America","wrong":["Africa","North America","Asia"]},{"id":"19df41f5c389","q":"Which of the following former Yugoslavian states is landlocked?","correct":"Serbia","wrong":["Bosnia and Herzegovina","Montenegro","Croatia"]},{"id":"6f06a432a1b4","q":"What year is on the flag of the US state Wisconsin?","correct":"1848","wrong":["1634","1783","1901"]},{"id":"1517cd67d477","q":"The historical city Timbuktu is located in which West African country?","correct":"Mali","wrong":["Senegal","Niger","Burkina Faso"]},{"id":"b1a5c416b353","q":"What is the capital of Indonesia?","correct":"Jakarta","wrong":["Bandung","Medan","Palembang"]},{"id":"00b31e449dc7","q":"The formerly East-Prussian city of Königsberg is known as which Russian City today?","correct":"Kaliningrad","wrong":["Kazan","Kursk","Krasnodar"]},{"id":"a087e2c23101","q":"Which of these is the name of the largest city in the US state Tennessee?","correct":"Memphis","wrong":["Thebes","Alexandria","Luxor"]},{"id":"b1f993499c15","q":"Where is Fort Marlborough located?","correct":"Bengkulu","wrong":["Singapore","London","Dover"]},{"id":"6a988d3230ce","q":"Which European city is known as the \"City of Light\"?","correct":"Paris","wrong":["Rome","London","Madrid"]},{"id":"4818e8535b73","q":"What is the right way to spell the capital of Hungary?","correct":"Budapest","wrong":["Boodapest","Bhudapest","Budapast"]},{"id":"7b778d6db671","q":"What was the original name of Ho Chi Minh City?","correct":"Saigon","wrong":["Hanoi","Dar Es Salaam","Angkor Wat"]},{"id":"b3dfae22a2d8","q":"What is the name of the former country that was succeeded by countries such as Serbia, Croatia and Slovenia?","correct":"Yugoslavia","wrong":["Czechoslovakia","Abkhazia","South Ossetia"]},{"id":"9b1e8e70afe6","q":"What is the largest lake in the African continent?","correct":"Lake Victoria","wrong":["Lake Tanganyika","Lake Malawi","Lake Turkana"]},{"id":"96ab335e3272","q":"Which nation claims ownership of Antarctica?","correct":"No one, but there are claims.","wrong":["United States of America","United Nations","Australia"]},{"id":"09be85108c35","q":"The land of Gotland is located in which European country?","correct":"Sweden","wrong":["Denmark","Norway","Germany"]},{"id":"2e7fc5926939","q":"Which is not a country in Africa?","correct":"Guyana","wrong":["Senegal","Liberia","Somalia"]},{"id":"d957b5ebc197","q":"How many sovereign states are members of the United Nations?","correct":"195","wrong":["201","153","178"]},{"id":"08f32e626df4","q":"Where are the Nazca Lines located?","correct":"Peru","wrong":["Brazil","Colombia","Ecuador"]},{"id":"e436f4693ac3","q":"What is the official language in Liechtenstein?","correct":"German","wrong":[