y countries used to be known as the region of Rhodesia between the 1890s and 1980?","correct":"Zambia & Zimbabwe","wrong":["Togo & Benin","Lesotho & Swaziland","Rwanda & Burundi"]},{"id":"2780bfa3adfe","q":"In which country is Tallinn located?","correct":"Estonia","wrong":["Finland","Sweden","Poland"]},{"id":"b29445edd879","q":"What is the capital of Seychelles?","correct":"Victoria","wrong":["Luanda","N'Djamena","Tripoli"]},{"id":"fc7d100e4618","q":"Which of the following languages does NOT use the Latin alphabet?","correct":"Georgian","wrong":["Turkish","Swahili","Vietnamese"]},{"id":"df428be7ec47","q":"What is the nickname for the US state Delaware?","correct":"The First State","wrong":["The Fiftieth State","The Second State","The Sixteenth State"]},{"id":"d50309f141dc","q":"What is the capital of Cyprus?","correct":"Nicosia","wrong":["Paphos","Limassol","Larnaca"]},{"id":"8d3cb56a6eb4","q":"What is the only state in the United States that does not have a flag in a shape with 4 edges?","correct":"Ohio","wrong":["Florida","Idaho","New Mexico"]},{"id":"950342299a4c","q":"A lion brandishing a sword is depicted on the national flag of which country?","correct":"Sri Lanka","wrong":["Albania","Zambia","Moldova"]},{"id":"1c9c3f770051","q":"Which small country is located between the borders of France and Spain?","correct":"Andorra","wrong":["San Marino","Vatican City","Lichtenstein"]},{"id":"addb7de5699e","q":"Which of these cities is NOT in England?","correct":"Edinburgh","wrong":["Oxford","Manchester","Southampton"]},{"id":"109fda62acbd","q":"What is the highest mountain in the world?","correct":"Mt. Everest","wrong":["Mount Godwin Austen","Kangchenjunga","Annapurna"]},{"id":"f510adc6c12e","q":"How tall is One World Trade Center in New York City?","correct":"1,776 ft","wrong":["1,888 ft","1,225 ft","1,960 ft"]},{"id":"6e464fdc94cc","q":"Which of the following geographic features is a ring-shaped coral reef, island, or series of islets?","correct":"Atoll","wrong":["Peni