"wrong":["New Guinea","Borneo","Madagascar"]},{"id":"e1ad70ead0cc","q":"When does Finland celebrate their independence day?","correct":"December 6th","wrong":["January 2nd","November 12th","February 8th"]},{"id":"c2ca2833f4c1","q":"The Suez Canal is located in which African country?","correct":"Egypt","wrong":["Libya","Ghana","Nigeria"]},{"id":"9736709400eb","q":"Where is the \"Sonoran Desert\" located?","correct":"North America","wrong":["South America","Asia","Africa"]},{"id":"5e48be404b0f","q":"What was the African nation of Zimbabwe formerly known as?","correct":"Rhodesia","wrong":["Zambia","Mozambique","Bulawayo"]},{"id":"632de5a46937","q":"Eritrea, which became the 182nd member of the UN in 1993, is in the continent of?","correct":"Africa","wrong":["Europe","Asia","South America"]}],"history":[{"id":"eb25f2c41140","q":"Which one of these rulers did not belong to the Habsburg dynasty?","correct":"Philip V","wrong":["Charles V","Philip II","Francis Joseph"]},{"id":"dcbeabf6a4a0","q":"When was \"The Gadget\", the first nuclear device to be detonated, tested?","correct":"July 16, 1945","wrong":["June 22, 1945","August 6, 1945","April 5, 1945"]},{"id":"f53f3c20116c","q":"What was the name of the chemical that was dropped on Vietnam during the Vietnam war?","correct":"Agent Orange","wrong":["Phosgene","Mustard Gas","Hydrogen Cyanide"]},{"id":"c0e6c45b31b7","q":"In which year did the First World War begin?","correct":"1914","wrong":["1930","1917","1939"]},{"id":"155ca992e342","q":"Who rode on horseback to warn the Minutemen that the British were coming during the U.S. Revolutionary War?","correct":"Paul Revere","wrong":["Thomas Paine","Henry Longfellow","Nathan Hale"]},{"id":"a59b1554d36b","q":"What is the name of the famous Apache leader who died in 1909 at the age of 70?","correct":"Geronimo","wrong":["Sitting Bull","Red Cloud","Crazy Horse"]},{"id":"af724251bf49","q":"What is the name of the US Navy spy ship which was attacked and captured by North Korean forces in 1968?","correct":"USS Pueblo","wrong":["USS North Carolina","USS Constitution","USS Indianapolis"]},{"id":"222a1d38e04c","q":"Which historical conflict killed the most people?","correct":"World War II","wrong":["Taiping Rebellion","Three Kingdoms War","Mongol conquests"]},{"id":"3353d14fcc70","q":"Which of these landmarks is not included in the original 'Seven Wonders of the Ancient World'?","correct":"Great Wall of China","wrong":["Great Pyramid of Giza","Colossus of Rhodes","Hanging Gardens of Babylon"]},{"id":"fd472edf9838","q":"How was Socrates executed?","correct":"Poison","wrong":["Decapitation","Firing squad","Crucifixion"]},{"id":"bf372c28d751","q":"Who is the creator of the soft drink, Dr. Pepper?","correct":"Charles Alderton","wrong":["James Wellington","Johnson Hinsin","Boris Heviltik"]},{"id":"a74f5e386860","q":"During the Roman Triumvirate of 42 BCE, what region of the Roman Republic was given to Lepidus?","correct":"Hispania","wrong":["Italia","Gallia","Asia"]},{"id":"6af95e459f90","q":"In which year was Nelson Mandela released from prison","correct":"1990","wrong":["1994","1992","1980"]},{"id":"a929f6b0e628","q":"Hong Kong was a part of which country's territory before Britain regained it in 1945?","correct":"Japan","wrong":["China","Phillipines","French Indonesia"]},{"id":"284973935466","q":"In which one of these cities did the Great Stink of 1858 occur?","correct":"London","wrong":["Berlin","New York","Moscow"]},{"id":"240b0c5de750","q":"The main objective of the German operation \"Case Blue\" during World War II was originally to capture what?","correct":"Caucasus","wrong":["Stalingrad","Crimea","Voronezh"]},{"id":"2dd84b5d972e","q":"Before the American colonies switched to the Gregorian calendar in 1752, on what date did their new year start?","correct":"March 25th","wrong":["June 1st","September 25th","December 1st"]},{"id":"ed26cb38961c","q":"Which of the following African countries was most successful in resisting colonization?","correct":"Ethiopia","wrong":["C&ocirc;te d’Ivoire","Congo","Namibia"]},{"id":"5571539feb51","q":"What war did George Orwell famously volunteer for and nearly died in?","correct":"Spanish Civil War","wrong":["World War I","World War II","Russian Civil War"]},{"id":"434bc2e3739e","q":"Which modern country is known as \"The Graveyard of Empires\"?","correct":"Afghanistan","wrong":["China","Iraq","Russia"]},{"id":"13922575fa52","q":"Which U.S. president took part in the Potsdam Conference, where the Allies reached a peace settlement with Germany?","correct":"Harry S. Truman","wrong":["Dwight D. Eisenhower","Franklin D. Roosevelt","Herbert Hoover"]},{"id":"92e49ee3f959","q":"Where did first known lesbian rights organization in the United States, Daughters of Bilitis, start?","correct":"San Francisco","wrong":["New York","Chicago","Los Angeles"]},{"id":"9ac3fc321bac","q":"What was the total length of the Titanic?","correct":"882 ft | 268.8 m","wrong":["759 ft | 231.3 m","1042 ft | 317.6 m","825 ft | 251.5 m"]},{"id":"b80cc9a2d5b2","q":"What day did the Battle of Gettysburg begin?","correct":"July 1, 1863","wrong":["September 17, 1862","July 21, 1861","Apr 30, 1863"]},{"id":"f8bf4c4dda0b","q":"Which country gifted the Statue of Liberty to the United States of America?","correct":"France","wrong":["Spain","England","Germany"]},{"id":"be522d1dc78b","q":"Which Louis was known as 'The Sun King of France'?","correct":"Louis XIV","wrong":["Louis XIII","Louis XV","Louis XVI"]},{"id":"89157e62eead","q":"In what year did William the Conqueror take control of England?","correct":"1066","wrong":["1123","1205","901"]},{"id":"94aba2fcdc9d","q":"When was Napoleon Bonaparte crowned emperor of the French?","correct":"December 2nd 1804","wrong":["July 3rd 1802","March 8th 1803","October 15th 1804"]},{"id":"9023f7f06e6f","q":"On which day did the attempted coup d'etat of 1991 in the Soviet Union begin?","correct":"August 19","wrong":["August 21","December 26","December 24"]},{"id":"d4280b6d2538","q":"The original Roman alphabet lacked the following letters EXCEPT:","correct":"X","wrong":["W","U","J"]},{"id":"bdbd5965dd13","q":"Who assassinated President James A. Garfield?","correct":"Charles Guiteau","wrong":["Sirhan Sirhan","Leon Czolgosz","John Wilkes Booth"]},{"id":"7e424a0b7d90","q":"When did the British hand-over sovereignty of Hong Kong back to China?","correct":"1997","wrong":["1999","1841","1900"]},{"id":"2eb5fc7613ae","q":"Joseph Smith was the founder of what religion?","correct":"Mormonism","wrong":["Buddhism","Christianity","Hinduism"]},{"id":"4bf07028e1fb","q":"In what year did Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin land on the moon?","correct":"1969","wrong":["1965","1966","1973"]},{"id":"be239ac035f5","q":"When was the Gregorian Calendar first adopted?","correct":"1582","wrong":["1623","1501","1555"]},{"id":"973b1d350039","q":"Which Apollo mission was the last one in NASA's Apollo program?","correct":"Apollo 17","wrong":["Apollo 13","Apollo 11","Apollo 15"]},{"id":"e3925bd87e66","q":"What age was King Henry V when he died?","correct":"35","wrong":["62","87","73"]},{"id":"dbe23f25c3f0","q":"Who assassinated Archduke Franz Ferdinand?","correct":"Gavrilo Princip","wrong":["Nedeljko Čabrinović","Oskar Potiorek","Ferdinand Cohen-Blind"]},{"id":"936120abf32c","q":"Who was the only US President to be elected four times?","correct":"Franklin Roosevelt","wrong":["Theodore Roosevelt","George Washington","Abraham Lincoln"]},{"id":"50a09264bebb","q":"Who was the first emperor of Rome?","correct":"Augustus","wrong":["Julius Caesar","Pompey Magnus","Claudius"]},{"id":"236414bdde2c","q":"What was Manfred von Richthofen's nickname?","correct":"The Red Baron","wrong":["The High Flying Ace","The Blue Serpent","The Germany Gunner"]},{"id":"cfc3fc824d8a","q":"What was the first sport to have been played on the moon?","correct":"Golf","wrong":["Football","Tennis","Soccer"]},{"id":"01216abf44bc","q":"In which years did the Battle of Gallipoli take place?","correct":"1915 - 1916","wrong":["1914 - 1918","1914 - 1915","1915 - 1918"]},{"id":"7fb806228236","q":"What is the name given to the series of confrontations between the UK and Iceland over North Atlantic fishing rights?","correct":"The Cod Wars","wrong":["The Lobster Wars","The Halibut Wars","The Mackerel Wars"]},{"id":"bb21e3f1191d","q":"What was the Canada's first capital?","correct":"Kingston","wrong":["Toronto","Ottawa","Montreal"]},{"id":"c627ae239236","q":"When was the city of Rome, Italy founded?","correct":"753 BCE","wrong":["902 BCE","524 BCE","697 BCE"]},{"id":"2b62bc2f670b","q":"All of the following are names of the Seven Warring States EXCEPT:","correct":"Zhai (翟)","wrong":["Zhao (趙)","Qin (秦)","Qi (齊)"]},{"id":"a577b7ffe017","q":"Which of the following countries was the first to send an object into space?","correct":"Germany","wrong":["USA","Russia","China"]},{"id":"2393953a2f51","q":"How did the Vikings call their short-lived colony in today's Canada?","correct":"V&iacute;nland","wrong":["F&oslash;royar","H&aring;logaland","Sk&aring;ne"]},{"id":"03dfb2a6bf1c","q":"Who was the leader of Sweden in the Great Northern War?","correct":"Charles XII","wrong":["Per Albin Hansson","Peter the Great","Gustavus Adolphus"]},{"id":"b45241df4db6","q":"What year did the Battle of Agincourt take place?","correct":"1415","wrong":["1463","1401","1422"]},{"id":"472cb93df2d9","q":"When was the United States National Security Agency established?","correct":"November 4, 1952","wrong":["July 26, 1908","July 1, 1973","November 25, 2002"]},{"id":"e1256cdc6270","q":"Which country was Josef Stalin born in?","correct":"Georgia","wrong":["Russia","Germany","Poland"]},{"id":"d1a84e5e9443","q":"Who is believed to have been the first European to 'discover' the land of New Zealand?","correct":"Abel Tasman","wrong":["Christopher Columbus","Jeanne Baré","John Cabot"]},{"id":"e11f02a49e8e","q":"When did the Crisis of the Third Century begin?","correct":"235 AD","wrong":["235 BC","242 AD","210 AD"]},{"id":"3aedbee8f021","q":"What did the abbreviation \"RMS\" stand for in the RMS Titanic in 1912?","correct":"Royal Mail Ship","wrong":["Royal Majesty Service","Regular Maritime Schedule","Regulated Maelstrom Sensor"]},{"id":"d59ed0e7830c","q":"What year did the Vietnam War end?","correct":"1975","wrong":["1978","1967","1969"]},{"id":"654b88d7d88c","q":"What historical event was Tchaikovsky's 1812 Overture referencing?","correct":"The Napoleonic Wars","wrong":["The American War of 1812","The Russian Revolution","The Charge of the Light Brigade (Crimean War)"]},{"id":"7887f19fa2cb","q":"What was the aim of the \"Umbrella Revolution\" in Hong Kong in 2014?","correct":"Genuine universal suffrage","wrong":["Gaining Independence","Go back under British Rule","Lower taxes"]},{"id":"80c9627dde6a","q":"What was the bloodiest single-day battle during the American Civil War?","correct":"The Battle of Antietam","wrong":["The Siege of Vicksburg","The Battle of Gettysburg","The Battles of Chancellorsville"]},{"id":"c88bc854874b","q":"Which U.S. President was in office when the Gulf War began?","correct":"George H. W. Bush","wrong":["Richard Nixon","George W. Bush","Ronald Regan"]},{"id":"5ba4b7d64c77","q":"The 15th century conflicts between the Houses of York and Lancaster are known as the Wars of the what?","correct":"Wars of the Roses","wrong":["Wars of the Lillies","Wars of the Daffodils","Wars of the Tulips"]},{"id":"e75424817495","q":"Which King of England was faced with the Peasants' Revolt in 1381?","correct":"Richard II","wrong":["Edward III","Edward II","Henry IV"]},{"id":"e0bae14ddabb","q":"The Thirty Years War ended with which treaty?","correct":"Peace of Westphalia","wrong":["Treaty of Versailles","Treaty of Paris","Peace of Prague"]},{"id":"875288c7d231","q":"The creator of the Enigma Cypher and Machine was of what nationality?","correct":"German","wrong":["American","British","Polish"]},{"id":"8a1c24f57753","q":"The Hagia Sophia was commissioned by which emperor of the Byzantine Empire?","correct":"Justinian I","wrong":["Constantine IV","Arcadius","Theodosius the Great"]},{"id":"19c012bfcc45","q":"Which of these countries was sea charted in 1500 by the Portuguese maritime explorations?","correct":"Brazil","wrong":["India","Mozambique","Madagascar"]},{"id":"bafc5ba9fc24","q":"During which American Civil War campaign did Union troops dig a tunnel beneath Confederate troops to detonate explosives underneath them?","correct":"Siege of Petersburg","wrong":["Siege of Vicksburg","Antietam Campaign","Gettysburg Campagin"]},{"id":"21863ad46f3f","q":"When did Norway become free from Sweden?","correct":"1905","wrong":["1925","1814","1834"]},{"id":"b9ea9c15dac7","q":"The idea of Socialism was articulated and advanced by whom?","correct":"Karl Marx","wrong":["Vladimir Lenin","Joseph Stalin","Vladimir Putin"]},{"id":"54c6ea497123","q":"Who tutored Alexander the Great?","correct":"Aristotle","wrong":["Socrates","Plato","King Philip"]},{"id":"89d6378d7e1e","q":"What did the first vending machines in the early 1880's dispense?","correct":"Post cards","wrong":["Alcohol","Cigarettes","Sodas"]},{"id":"fec17d94b86c","q":"Which of the following Assyrian kings did NOT rule during the Neo-Assyrian Empire?","correct":"Shamshi-Adad III","wrong":["Shalmaneser V","Esharhaddon","Ashur-nasir-pal II"]},{"id":"d8236b758be6","q":"The Panama Canal was finished under the administration of which U.S. president?","correct":"Woodrow Wilson","wrong":["Franklin Delano Roosevelt","Herbert Hoover","Theodore Roosevelt"]},{"id":"f589a717ed6e","q":"In what prison was Adolf Hitler held in 1924?","correct":"Landsberg Prison","wrong":["Spandau Prison","Ebrach Abbey","Hohenasperg"]},{"id":"825eaac34089","q":"Pianist Frédéric Chopin was a composer of which musical era?","correct":"Romantic","wrong":["Classic","Baroque","Renaissance"]},{"id":"44212a51f324","q":"When did the French Revolution begin?","correct":"May 05 1789","wrong":["April 12 1789","April 05 1789","May 06 1799"]},{"id":"0e40a195e983","q":"What was the code name for the German invasion of the Soviet Union in WW2?","correct":"Operation Barbarossa","wrong":["Operation Kaiserschlact","Operation Unthinkable","Operation Molotov"]},{"id":"e5a4ee62b6a3","q":"According to legend, the ancient Greeks constructed a huge wooden model of which animal to gain entrance to Troy?","correct":"Horse","wrong":["Goat","Elephant","Wolf"]},{"id":"975a5db97b4d","q":"Which country was an allied power in World War II?","correct":"Soviet Union","wrong":["Italy","Germany","Japan"]},{"id":"cc5ed9d5c979","q":"The catastrophic nuclear accident that occurred in Ukraine in 1986 occurred at which power plant?","correct":"Chernobyl","wrong":["Ignalina","Mayak","Kursk"]},{"id":"68d16293f6cd","q":"Which of the following Presidents of the United States was assassinated?","correct":"William McKinley","wrong":["Lyndon Johnson","Chester Arthur","Franklin Roosevelt"]},{"id":"cbb89e4d6ad9","q":"Which of the following was not one of Joseph Stalin's ten blows during World War II?","correct":"Vistula-Oder Offensive","wrong":["Crimean Offensive","Leningrad-Novgorod Offensive","Operation Bagration"]},{"id":"0dcd69ce16ce","q":"Which of these facilities was not present on the Titanic?","correct":"Fainting room","wrong":["Turkish bath","Kennel","Squash court"]},{"id":"b2462596a51d","q":"The collapse of the Soviet Union took place in which year?","correct":"1991","wrong":["1992","1891","1990"]},{"id":"b5bfc0e19297","q":"What was the name of the German offensive operation in October 1941 to take Moscow before winter?","correct":"Operation Typhoon","wrong":["Operation Sunflower","Operation Barbarossa","Case Blue"]},{"id":"6d7a1ccdb502","q":"What was the original name of New York City?","correct":"New Amsterdam","wrong":["New London","New Paris","New Rome"]},{"id":"45ad180fb0c9","q":"What date was the first flight of the P-40 Warhawk?","correct":"October 14 1938","wrong":["August 21 1939","January 12 1940","June 1 1939"]},{"id":"ef40915524d6","q":"What is the historical name of Sri Lanka?","correct":"Ceylon","wrong":["Myanmar","Colombo","Badulla"]},{"id":"c48f6de21ccf","q":"What was found in 1946 by two young shepards near a cave?","correct":"Dead Sea Scrolls","wrong":["The Blackbeard Chest","Sheep","The First Oaxaca Cave Sleeper"]},{"id":"93b58c4a7ab4","q":"Who was the first man to travel into outer space?","correct":"Yuri Gagarin","wrong":["Virgil Ivan \"Gus\" Grissom","Neil Armstrong","Buzz Aldrin"]},{"id":"c0f671ab5586","q":"Toussaint Louverture led a successful slave revolt in which country?","correct":"Haiti","wrong":["France","Cuba","United States"]},{"id":"3141e4ffc159","q":"Which famous world leader is famed for the saying, \"Let them eat cake\", yet is rumored that he/she never said it at all?","correct":"Marie Antoinette","wrong":["Czar Nicholas II","Elizabeth I","Henry VIII"]},{"id":"b5479c0d63c4","q":"In which country was the Statue of Liberty built and exported to the United States of America?","correct":"France","wrong":["Germany","Spain","England"]},{"id":"881e297cca56","q":"What nationality was sultan Saladin?","correct":"Kurdish","wrong":["Arab","Egyptian","Syrian"]},{"id":"bc1b791f8b2b","q":"The Battle of Hastings was fought in which year?","correct":"1066","wrong":["911","1204","1420"]},{"id":"ac2967fc00f0","q":"When did Canada leave the confederation to become their own nation?","correct":"July 1st, 1867","wrong":["July 1st, 1763","July 1st, 1832","July 1st, 1902"]},{"id":"b266b5d46890","q":"What was the code name for the Allied invasion of Southern France on August 15th, 1944?","correct":"Operation Dragoon","wrong":["Operation Overlord","Operation Market Garden","Operation Torch"]},{"id":"de84760186e7","q":"Who was the first man to travel into outer space twice?","correct":"Gus Grissom","wrong":["Vladimir Komarov","Charles Conrad","Yuri Gagarin"]},{"id":"b6bd4a585266","q":"What was the last colony the UK ceded marking the end of the British Empire?","correct":"Hong Kong","wrong":["India","Australia","Ireland"]},{"id":"fe44fb57e192","q":"When was Adolf Hitler appointed as Chancellor of Germany?","correct":"January 30, 1933","wrong":["September 1, 1939","February 27, 1933","October 6, 1939"]},{"id":"b5213e0647f8","q":"How many Sister Ships were related to the TItanic?","correct":"2","wrong":["4","3","1"]},{"id":"0535be57abc3","q":"Which Las Vegas casino was originally constructed and operated by mobster Bugsy Siegel?","correct":"The Flamingo","wrong":["The MGM Grand","The Sands","The Sahara"]},{"id":"9bbd0abf6fe6","q":"The Battle of the Somme in World War I took place in which country?","correct":"France","wrong":["Germany","Italy","Austria"]},{"id":"6be7ff5a07c2","q":"What is the name of the ship which was only a few miles away from the RMS Titanic when it struck an iceberg on April 14, 1912?","correct":"Californian","wrong":["Carpathia","Cristol","Commerce"]},{"id":"e9fd76ab0596","q":"After the 1516 Battle of Marj Dabiq, the Ottoman Empire took control of Jerusalem from which sultanate?","correct":"Mamluk","wrong":["Ayyubid","Ummayyad","Seljuq"]},{"id":"cb5ec7f325de","q":"In which year did the Invasion of Kuwait by Iraq occur?","correct":"1990","wrong":["1992","1988","1986"]},{"id":"222dc2aed974","q":"The ontological argument for the proof of God's existence is first attributed to whom?","correct":"Anselm of Canterbury","wrong":["René Descartes","Immanuel Kant","Aristotle"]},{"id":"d86df2a68761","q":"When did O, Canada officially become the national anthem?","correct":"1980","wrong":["1950","1920","1880"]},{"id":"ef1f041e6b9b","q":"The first Legoland park was opened in 1968 in which of these cities?","correct":"Billund, Denmark","wrong":["Carlsbad, California","Winter Haven, Florida","Nagoya, Japan"]},{"id":"73586b0add14","q":"In the Seven Wonders of the World, which wonder is the only that has survived to this day?","correct":"Great Pyramid of Giza","wrong":["Colossus of Rhodes","Lighthouse of Alexandria","Statue of Zeus at Olympia"]},{"id":"efcc7cd1d0ae","q":"Abolitionist John Brown raided the arsenal in which Virginia Town?","correct":"Harper's Ferry","wrong":["Richmond","Harrisonburg","Martinsburg"]},{"id":"f01ef6a4374e","q":"Which of these theoretical phycisists first predicted the existence of antimatter?","correct":"Paul Dirac","wrong":["Niels Bohr","Albert Einstein","Werner Heisenberg"]},{"id":"6344aa01033d","q":"What year did World War I begin?","correct":"1914","wrong":["1905","1919","1925"]},{"id":"2f5173e78891","q":"What is the bloodiest event in United States history, in terms of casualties?","correct":"Battle of Antietam","wrong":["Pearl Harbor","September 11th","D-Day"]},{"id":"d64d7f423d05","q":"In 1453, which important city fell?","correct":"Constantinople","wrong":["Rome","Hamburg","Athens"]},{"id":"94cf15ddf086","q":"The Herero genocide was perpetrated in Africa by which of the following colonial nations?","correct":"Germany","wrong":["Britain","Belgium","France"]},{"id":"82c9084a82b5","q":"How many years did the Hundred Years' War last?","correct":"116","wrong":["100","90","101"]},{"id":"1a54102b08b0","q":"In World War I, what was the name of the alliance of Germany, Austria-Hungary, the Ottoman Empire, and Bulgaria?","correct":"The Central Powers","wrong":["The Axis Powers","The Federation of Empires","Authoritarian Alliance"]},{"id":"6b8c8644763c","q":"In what year did the Wall Street Crash take place?","correct":"1929","wrong":["1932","1930","1925"]},{"id":"0836c2a03d3a","q":"What was Napoleon Bonaparte's name before he changed it?","correct":"Napoleone di Buonaparte","wrong":["Naapolion van Bonijpaart","Napole&atilde;o do Boaparte","Napoleona de Buenoparte"]},{"id":"f01377bc9206","q":"Which country had an \"Orange Revolution\" between 2004 and 2005?","correct":"Ukraine","wrong":["Belarus","Latvia","Lithuania"]},{"id":"3052284be326","q":"As poverty and racial tensions pushed African-Americans out of the southern US, many of them moved north in an event known as what?","correct":"The Great Migration","wrong":["The Great Awakening","The Harlem Renaissance","The Resettlement"]},{"id":"b00570ed03ad","q":"Which of the following ancient peoples was NOT classified as Hellenic (Greek)?","correct":"Illyrians","wrong":["Dorians","Achaeans","Ionians"]},{"id":"f69f1bf78f0d","q":"In 1961, an American B-52 aircraft crashed and nearly detonated two 4mt nuclear bombs over which US city?","correct":"Goldsboro, North Carolina","wrong":["Hicksville, New York","Jacksonville, Florida","Conway, Arkansas"]},{"id":"fa02ecf7730e","q":"When did Vesuvius destroy the city of Pompeii?","correct":"79 AD","wrong":["62 AD","31 BC","54 BC"]},{"id":"766552ff42b9","q":"Who led the Communist Revolution of Russia?","correct":"Vladimir Lenin","wrong":["Joseph Stalin","Vladimir Putin","Mikhail Gorbachev"]},{"id":"7e92296960df","q":"What did Albert Einstein win the Nobel Prize for in 1921?","correct":"Photoelectric Effect","wrong":["Relativity","Wave-Particle Duality","Zero-Point Energy"]},{"id":"af43095ef19a","q":"Which South American country fought Great Britain over the Falkland Islands in 1982?","correct":"Argentina","wrong":["Brazil","Chile","Venezuela"]},{"id":"964029ad8545","q":"What micro-state is considered to have the oldest constitution still in effect?","correct":"San Marino","wrong":["Andorra","Monaco","Saint Kitts and Nevis"]},{"id":"c8ae5e49b859","q":"Which country attacked the USS Liberty on June 8, 1967?","correct":"Israel","wrong":["Syria","Saudi Arabia","Iran"]},{"id":"8cf585b4881c","q":"The \"Trail of Tears\" was a result of which United States President's Indian Removal Policy?","correct":"Andrew Jackson","wrong":["Harry S. Truman","Martin Van Buren","John Quincy Adams"]},{"id":"f36bc1cd92a2","q":"How many times was Albert Einstein married in his lifetime?","correct":"Twice","wrong":["Five","Thrice","Once"]},{"id":"c1d1a3d9162d","q":"Who was the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom for most of World War II?","correct":"Winston Churchill","wrong":["Neville Chamberlain","Harold Macmillan","Edward Heath"]},{"id":"15c665e1a03c","q":"Where and when was the first cardboard box made for industrial use?","correct":"England, 1817","wrong":["United States, 1817","England, 1917","United States, 1917"]},{"id":"13e07de66fb8","q":"On which day did construction start on \"The Pentagon\", the headquarters for the United States Department of Defense?","correct":"September 11, 1941","wrong":["June 15, 1947","January 15, 1943","September 2, 1962"]},{"id":"2ce779fa8b0c","q":"After his loss at the Battle of Waterloo, Napoleon Bonaparte was exiled to which island?","correct":"St. Helena","wrong":["Elba","Corsica","Canary"]},{"id":"f297c06d802b","q":"Who famously coined the phrase \"I think, therefore I am\"?","correct":"Descartes","wrong":["Plato","Aristotle","Shakespeare"]},{"id":"5fb5fa816c1e","q":"The son of which pope supposedly held a lecherous f&ecirc;te involving 50 courtesans in the papal palace?","correct":"Alexander VI","wrong":["Innocent V","Urban II","Pius III"]},{"id":"c6db39ba6791","q":"The Arab Spring was a series of protests and rebellions that began in which of these Arab nations?","correct":"Tunisia","wrong":["Morocco","Syria","Egypt"]},{"id":"3f546d85eb03","q":"What was the name commonly given to the ancient trade routes that connected the East and West of Eurasia?","correct":"Silk Road","wrong":["Spice Road","Clay Road","Salt Road"]},{"id":"a68133d272a9","q":"When was the SS or Schutzstaffel established?","correct":"April 4th, 1925","wrong":["September 1st, 1941","March 8th, 1935","February 21st, 1926"]},{"id":"b82572522830","q":"The crown of the Empire State Building was originally built for what purpose?","correct":"Airship Dock","wrong":["Lightning Rod","Antennae","Flag Pole"]},{"id":"524fb7a71cf0","q":"The United States Army Air Corps became the United States Air Force on what date?","correct":"September 18, 1947","wrong":["December 14, 1946","October 27, 1945","November 08, 1944"]},{"id":"969233e42788","q":"Who was the last Roman emperor in the Year of Four Emperors (69 AD)?","correct":"Vespasian","wrong":["Vitellius","Otho","Galba"]},{"id":"b6df25c3b4b7","q":"On what street did the 1666 Great Fire of London start?","correct":"Pudding Lane","wrong":["Baker Street","Houses of Parliament","St Paul's Cathedral"]},{"id":"e70af9eb0895","q":"What year was Canada founded in?","correct":"1867","wrong":["1798","1859","1668"]},{"id":"8d3bc56dedc6","q":"In 1720, England was in massive debt and became involved in the South Sea Bubble. Who was the main mastermind behind it?","correct":"John Blunt","wrong":["Daniel Defoe","Robert Harley","John Churchill"]},{"id":"f104bb9f2795","q":"Where was Abraham Lincoln when he was assassinated by John Wilkes Booth in 1865?","correct":"At the theatre","wrong":["On a boat","On his horse","In bed"]},{"id":"d29ec8348473","q":"When was Google founded?","correct":"September 4, 1998","wrong":["October 9, 1997","December 12, 1989","Feburary 7th, 2000"]},{"id":"d041e5eba8b6","q":"When did Lithuania declare independence from the Soviet Union?","correct":"March 11th, 1990","wrong":["December 25th, 1991","December 5th, 1991","April 20th, 1989"]},{"id":"e9c575ae3e37","q":"Who was the first prime minister of Canada?","correct":"John Macdonald","wrong":["John Abbott","Alexander Mackenzie","Robert Borden"]},{"id":"33dba612d32f","q":"What is widely considered to be the oldest civilization known to mankind?","correct":"Sumeria","wrong":["Babylon","Assyria","Phoenicia"]},{"id":"e2ce71eb48ac","q":"Who was a military strategist in the Eastern Zhou period?","correct":"Sun Tzu","wrong":["Lu Bu","Genghis Khan","Vlad The Impaler"]},{"id":"4a066cdd4fd9","q":"What was the first recorded object to ever reach space?","correct":"Bumper-WAC","wrong":["American Manhole Cover","Sputnik I","Sputnik II"]},{"id":"afc0801ea9ec","q":"During the Wars of the Roses (1455 - 1487) which Englishman was dubbed \"the Kingmaker\"?","correct":"Richard Neville","wrong":["Richard III","Henry V","Thomas Warwick"]},{"id":"5c4405309b8a","q":"The Ottoman Empire was dissolved after their loss in which war?","correct":"World War I","wrong":["Crimean War","Serbian Revolution","Second Balkan War"]},{"id":"f334afa3de71","q":"Which of these countries remained neutral during World War II?","correct":"Switzerland","wrong":["United Kingdom","France","Italy"]},{"id":"3d62061f8bbb","q":"In what year was the M1911 pistol designed?","correct":"1911","wrong":["1907","1899","1917"]},{"id":"7fec29d498cb","q":"Which of the following physicists did NOT work on the Manhattan project?","correct":"Murray Gell-Mann","wrong":["Richard Feynman","J. Robert Oppenheimer","John Von-Neumann"]},{"id":"6dcbc8de46b7","q":"Which is the hull NO. of the Fletcher class destroyer Fletcher?","correct":"DD-445","wrong":["DD-992","DD-444","DD-446"]},{"id":"8cc757640791","q":"When was Finland's 100th year of being independent?","correct":"2017","wrong":["2016","2018","2015"]},{"id":"bba1978be35a","q":"Which Greek god was the god of the Sun?","correct":"Helios","wrong":["Zeus","Hades","Poseidon"]},{"id":"52dac39c0a83","q":"What year did Skoal, a smokeless Tobacco company, release their first line of Pouches, known as \"Skoal Bandits\"?","correct":"1983","wrong":["1934","1984","1822"]},{"id":"d66052542303","q":"Who was the first president born in the independent United States?","correct":"Martin Van Buren","wrong":["John Adams","George Washington","James Monroe"]},{"id":"0aff6c2033a7","q":"What year were the Marian Reforms instituted in the Roman Republic?","correct":"107 BCE","wrong":["42 BCE","264 BCE","102 CE"]},{"id":"b097f3c4d9f0","q":"One of the deadliest pandemics, the \"Spanish Flu\", killed off what percentage of the human world population at the time?","correct":"3 to 6 percent","wrong":["6 to 10 percent","1 to 3 percent","less than 1 percent"]},{"id":"a9daf12ebdf3","q":"When was the People's Republic of China founded?","correct":"October 1, 1949","wrong":["April 3, 1947","May 7, 1945","December 6, 1950"]},{"id":"2fee6b66ffe9","q":"Which one of these countries was NOT in the Central Powers during WWI?","correct":"Spain","wrong":["Austria-Hungary","Turkey","Germany"]},{"id":"999a95303872","q":"Who was the main developer of the Suez Canal?","correct":"Ferdinand de Lesseps","wrong":["Louis-Eugène Cavaignac","John Milton","Johann Lukas von Hildebrandt"]},{"id":"7deb2933ed33","q":"During the Mongolian invasions of Japan, what were the Mongol boats mostly stopped by?","correct":"Typhoons","wrong":["Tornados","Economic depression","Samurai"]},{"id":"9bdc8c8bf148","q":"Which infamous European traitor was known as \"the last person to enter Parliament with honest intentions\"?","correct":"Guy Fawkes","wrong":["Robert Catesby","Francis Tresham","Everard Digby"]},{"id":"4c176142eb82","q":"What was the name of the African-American cultural explosion centered in upper Manhattan during the 1920s and 1930s?","correct":"Harlem Renaissance","wrong":["Inwood Renaissance","Bed-Stuy Renaissance","Upper East Renaissance"]},{"id":"2655e6c80b3d","q":"Which U.S. president was said to have been too honest to lie to his father about chopping down a cherry tree?","correct":"George Washington","wrong":["Abraham Lincoln","Thomas Jefferson","James Monroe"]},{"id":"f00ecb5b1a6b","q":"On which aircraft carrier did the Doolitte Raid launch from on April 18, 1942 during World War II?","correct":"USS Hornet","wrong":["USS Enterprise","USS Lexington","USS Saratoga"]},{"id":"68be42e34eff","q":"In what year did the Berlin Wall fall?","correct":"1989","wrong":["1987","1991","1993"]},{"id":"2ab0ad0e4e66","q":"What was the name of one of the surviving palaces of Henry VIII located near Richmond, London?","correct":"Hampton Court","wrong":["St James's Palace","Buckingham Palace","Coughton Court"]},{"id":"aecd663497bc","q":"Who was the British Prime Minister at the outbreak of the Second World War in 1939?","correct":"Neville Chamberlain","wrong":["Stanley Baldwin","Winston Churchill","Ramsay MacDonald"]},{"id":"e1ee1aa56ad4","q":"Which of these founding fathers of the United States of America later became president?","correct":"James Monroe","wrong":["Alexander Hamilton","Samuel Adams","Roger Sherman"]},{"id":"4bde4ef1e109","q":"Which of the following snipers has the highest amount of confirmed kills?","correct":"Simo Häyhä","wrong":["Chris Kyle","Vasily Zaytsev","Craig Harrison"]},{"id":"ca34b51ad894","q":"What was the transfer of disease, crops, and people across the Atlantic shortly after the discovery of the Americas called?","correct":"The Columbian Exchange","wrong":["Triangle Trade","Transatlantic Slave Trade","The Silk Road"]},{"id":"48e6717ecc27","q":"Which day did World War I begin?","correct":"July 28","wrong":["January 28","June 28","April 28"]},{"id":"7e35d5517175","q":"What event marked the start of World War II?","correct":"Invasion of Poland (1939)","wrong":["Invasion of Russia (1942)","Battle of Britain (1940)","Invasion of Normandy (1944)"]},{"id":"820d80b15768","q":"In what year did the North American Video Game Crash occur?","correct":"1983","wrong":["1982","1993","1970"]},{"id":"01495b878f22","q":"Which country did the Eureka Rebellion, an 1856 battle against colonial rule, take place in?","correct":"Australia","wrong":["India","Canada","Brazil"]},{"id":"d517133eb1e3","q":"John Moses Browning, the designer of the M1918 BAR (Browning Automatic Rifle) was a part of which religion?","correct":"Mormon","wrong":["Catholic","Jewish","Atheist"]},{"id":"3680cfc341ba","q":"The Second Boer War in 1899 was fought where?","correct":"South Africa","wrong":["Argentina","Nepal","Bulgaria"]},{"id":"0081e0b7aea1","q":"Which American civilization is the source of the belief that the world would end or drastically change on December 21st, 2012?","correct":"The Mayans","wrong":["The Incas","The Aztecs","The Navajos"]},{"id":"2722e7d0605c","q":"What Russian automatic gas-operated assault rifle was developed in the Soviet Union in 1947, and is still popularly used today?","correct":"AK-47","wrong":["RPK","M16","MG 42"]},{"id":"52fcdd9e2e3a","q":"When did the Battle of the Bulge end?","correct":"January 25, 1945","wrong":["August 6, 1945","December 7, 1941","December 16, 1944"]},{"id":"5a66e2f0167c","q":"In what year was the video game company Electronic Arts founded?","correct":"1982","wrong":["1999","1981","2005"]},{"id":"f3cd25f53462","q":"Who invented the \"Flying Shuttle\" in 1738; one of the key developments in the industrialization of weaving?","correct":"John Kay","wrong":["James Hargreaves","Richard Arkwright","John Deere"]},{"id":"cc5c1afec142","q":"How old was Adolf Hitler when he died?","correct":"56","wrong":["43","65","47"]},{"id":"5a7c943e451f","q":"When was the Grand Patriotic War in the USSR concluded?","correct":"May 9th, 1945","wrong":["September 2nd, 1945","August 9th, 1945","December 11th, 1945"]},{"id":"72768b14122d","q":"In 1939, Britain and France declared war on Germany after it invaded which country?","correct":"Poland","wrong":["Czechoslovakia","Austria","Hungary"]},{"id":"825e0496afd0","q":"Who was the first mammal successfully launched into Earth's orbit?","correct":"Laika, the dog","wrong":["Ham, the chimpanzee","Baker, the monkey","Belka, the dog"]},{"id":"7a657785c053","q":"When did Jamaica receive its independence from England?","correct":"1962","wrong":["1492","1963","1987"]},{"id":"38cb18a94adf","q":"A collection of Sanskrit hymns and verses known as the Vedas are sacred texts in what religion?","correct":"Hinduism","wrong":["Judaism","Islam","Buddhism"]},{"id":"fd0fa07563d0","q":"During WWII, in 1945, the United States dropped atomic bombs on the two Japanese cities of Hiroshima and what other city?","correct":"Nagasaki","wrong":["Kawasaki","Tokyo","Kagoshima"]},{"id":"6db643e8b00f","q":"What was the name of the spy ring that helped the United States win the Revolutionary War?","correct":"Culper Ring","wrong":["New York Spy Ring","Washington's Spies","Unnamed"]},{"id":"88c45d21b158","q":"What Southeast Asian country was formerly known as 'Lan Xang'?","correct":"Laos","wrong":["Cambodia","Vietnam","Thailand"]},{"id":"c8337250d8ba","q":"In what year did the nuclear power plant in Chernobyl melt down?","correct":"1986","wrong":["1991","1975","1998"]},{"id":"7d12981cdaea","q":"Which of the following Soviet revolutionaries was exiled from the USSR and later assassinated in 1940 for criticizing Stalinism?","correct":"Leon Trotsky","wrong":["Lev Kamenev","Mikhail Kalinin","Vladimir Lenin"]},{"id":"592650271c45","q":"When is the Ides of March?","correct":"March 15","wrong":["March 14","March 31","March 1"]},{"id":"0f3590eb90b0","q":"Which of these positions did the astronomer and physicist Isaac Newton not hold?","correct":"Surveyor to the City of London","wrong":["Professor of Mathematics","Warden of the Royal Mint","Member of Parliament"]},{"id":"545454059b74","q":"Who was the first wife of King Henry VIII?","correct":"Catherine of Aragon","wrong":["Jane Seymour","Anne Boleyn","Anne of Cleves"]},{"id":"1ef2cacab3af","q":"In relation to the British Occupation in Ireland, what does the IRA stand for.","correct":"Irish Republican Army","wrong":["Irish Rebel Alliance","Irish Reformation Army","Irish-Royal Alliance"]},{"id":"dd306c68c1ad","q":"What year did World War II end?","correct":"1945","wrong":["1943","1947","1950"]},{"id":"e45b6225e933","q":"Which of the following is NOT classified as a Semetic language?","correct":"Sumerian","wrong":["Maltese","Akkadian","Mandaic"]},{"id":"28654d8cc500","q":"Which U.S. President was famously 'attacked' by a swimming rabbit?","correct":"Jimmy Carter","wrong":["Ronald Reagan","Lydon B. Johnson","Gerald Ford"]},{"id":"0459a65d983b","q":"King Henry VIII was the second monarch of which European royal house?","correct":"Tudor","wrong":["York","Stuart","Lancaster"]},{"id":"c78144de5bec","q":"Which one of these tanks was designed and operated by the United Kingdom?","correct":"Tog II","wrong":["M4 Sherman","Tiger H1","T-3