d":"233df1f4f8c8","q":"The seed drill was invented by which British inventor?","correct":"Jethro Tull","wrong":["Charles Babbage","Isaac Newton","J.J Thomson"]},{"id":"7a48d0270d8d","q":"Who led France during the \"Reign of Terror\" ?","correct":"Maximilien Robespierre","wrong":["Napoleon Bonaparte","Jean-Paul Marat","Louis XVI"]},{"id":"e20b11145d61","q":"Which WWII tank ace is credited with having destroyed the most tanks?","correct":"Kurt Knispel","wrong":["Michael Wittmann","Walter Kniep","Otto Carius"]},{"id":"78b3a810fb12","q":"The Korean War started in what year?","correct":"1950","wrong":["1945","1960","1912"]},{"id":"c8d0dc9c8ea5","q":"Under which name was Rodrigo Borgia made Pope?","correct":"Alexander VI","wrong":["Rodrigo I","John Paul II","Pius VII"]},{"id":"886e432a9580","q":"During what war did the \"Cuban Missile Crisis\" occur?","correct":"Cold War","wrong":["World War I","World War II","Revolutionary War"]},{"id":"e1afa4eff250","q":"What is the name of the Boeing B-29 that dropped the 'Little Boy' atomic bomb on Hiroshima?","correct":"Enola Gay","wrong":["Necessary Evil","The Great Artiste","Full House"]},{"id":"5c158d2d6f25","q":"During the Spanish Civil War (1936), Francisco Franco fought for which political faction?","correct":"Nationalist Spain","wrong":["Republican Spain","Popular Front","Papal State"]},{"id":"1e93dababff2","q":"The coat of arms of the King of Spain contains the arms from the monarchs of Castille, Leon, Aragon and which other former Iberian kingdom?","correct":"Navarre","wrong":["Galicia","Granada","Catalonia"]},{"id":"190d87787402","q":"What is the oldest US state?","correct":"Delaware","wrong":["Rhode Island","Maine","Virginia"]},{"id":"6bbbb2f977e9","q":"What is the mnemonic device for remembering the fates of the wives of Henry VIII?","correct":"Divorced, Beheaded, Died, Divorced, Beheaded, Survived","wrong":["Beheaded, Died, Divorced, Divorced, Beheaded, Survived","Died, Beheaded, Divorced, Beheaded, Survived, Divorced","Survived, Beheaded, Died, Divorced, Divorced, Beheaded"]},{"id":"2026401b27a8","q":"What was the capital of South Vietnam before the Vietnam War?","correct":"Saigon","wrong":["Ho Chi Minh City","Hanoi","Hue"]},{"id":"cc3f0409a7ef","q":"What was Genghis Khan's real name?","correct":"Temüjin","wrong":["Möngke","&Ouml;gedei","Temür"]},{"id":"1aea8b2a251b","q":"How long did World War II last?","correct":"6 years","wrong":["4 years","5 years","7 years"]},{"id":"4e569aa3afda","q":"When did construction of the Suez Canal finish?","correct":"1869","wrong":["1859","1860","1850"]},{"id":"ff396f81ffa1","q":"Who was the first President of the People's Republic of China?","correct":"Mao Zedong","wrong":["Liu Shaoqi","Dong Biwu","Li Xiannian"]},{"id":"1d6273bf0fc2","q":"Where was Napoleon Bonaparte born?","correct":"Corsica","wrong":["Normandy","Brittany","Paris"]},{"id":"a2f25576f0df","q":"Who was the leader of the Communist Party of Yugoslavia ?","correct":"Josip Broz Tito","wrong":["Karadjordje Petrovic","Milos Obilic","Aleskandar Petrovic"]},{"id":"bd4c402d0d47","q":"What year did Australia become a federation?","correct":"1901","wrong":["1910","1899","1911"]},{"id":"328fd814caab","q":"What was the official German currency until 2002?","correct":"Mark","wrong":["Frank","Pound sterling","Reichtoken"]},{"id":"20b6251ab25e","q":"What was William Frederick Cody better known as?","correct":"Buffalo Bill","wrong":["Billy the Kid","Wild Bill Hickok","Pawnee Bill"]},{"id":"ff9b96397951","q":"When was the \"Siege of Leningrad\" lifted during World War II?","correct":"January 1944","wrong":["September 1943","November 1943","March 1944"]},{"id":"ccb688b75bf7","q":"What country joined the EU in 2013?","correct":"Croatia","wrong":["Bulgaria","Slovenia","Turkey"]},{"id":"a744ba4f09b0","q":"Who was the first explorer to sail to North America?","correct":"Leif Erikson","wrong":["Christopher Columbus","Amerigo Vespucci","Ferdinand Magellan"]},{"id":"eff1c5030422","q":"Which of the following Physicists aided Nazi Germany in their production of a nuclear weapon?","correct":"Werner Heisenberg","wrong":["John von Neumann","Albert Einstein","Max Planck"]},{"id":"573528c47804","q":"Which German field marshal was known as the `Desert Fox`?","correct":"Erwin Rommel","wrong":["Ernst Busch","Wolfram Freiherr von Richthofen","Wilhelm List"]},{"id":"8d123ea4373d","q":"The Bohemian Revolt (1618-1620) started after Protestants in Prague did what to their Catholic Lords Regents?","correct":"Threw them out of a window","wrong":["Insulted their mothers","Locked them in stockades","Hung them."]},{"id":"f275210c8171","q":"Who was the last emperor of Mexico?","correct":"Ferdinand Maximilian","wrong":["Andrés Manuel L&oacute;pez Obrador","Napoleon III","Agust&iacute;n de Iturbide"]},{"id":"97127fb761ad","q":"What year did the Boxing Day earthquake & tsunami occur in the Indian Ocean?","correct":"2004","wrong":["2006","2008","2002"]},{"id":"d262257ecfc0","q":"What number does the Roman numeral \"D\" stand for?","correct":"500","wrong":["100","1000","50"]},{"id":"be2c68ec2fc6","q":"Which of these countries was NOT a part of the Soviet Union?","correct":"Afghanistan","wrong":["Turkmenistan","Kazakhstan","Uzbekistan"]},{"id":"6b04a405c0ea","q":"Who succeded Josef Stalin as the leader of the Soviet Union?","correct":"Nikita Krushchev","wrong":["Lavrentiy Beria","Vyacheslav Molotov","Georgy Malenkov"]},{"id":"9847aaedc6aa","q":"Which English king was married to Eleanor of Aquitaine?","correct":"Henry II","wrong":["Richard I","Henry I","Henry V"]},{"id":"d4656e7e6c7d","q":"When Christopher Columbus sailed to America, what was the first region he arrived in?","correct":"The Bahamas Archipelago","wrong":["Florida","Isthmus of Panama","Nicaragua"]},{"id":"ca288f08e123","q":"Which of the following ancient Near Eastern peoples still exists as a modern ethnic group?","correct":"Assyrians","wrong":["Babylonians","Hittites","Elamites"]},{"id":"dd09a125ecf2","q":"What year was the first Pizza Hut restaurant opened?","correct":"1958","wrong":["1976","1965","1942"]},{"id":"abd19840743a","q":"What year is considered to be the year that the British Empire ended?","correct":"1997","wrong":["1986","1981","1971"]},{"id":"33242191b5c1","q":"In which year did the Tokyo Subway Sarin Attack occur?","correct":"1995","wrong":["2001","2011","1991"]},{"id":"3016e605682d","q":"Which Roman Emperor led the Roman Empire to reach its maximum territorial extent?","correct":"Trajan","wrong":["Julius Caesar","Claudius","Constantine the Great"]},{"id":"2a4bb440993c","q":"What were the first states to break away from Yugoslavia?","correct":"Slovenia, Croatia","wrong":["Macedonia, Montenegro","Slovenia, Macedonia","Montenegro, Slovenia"]},{"id":"b7f6e9a7802b","q":"In the War of the Pacific (1879 - 1883), Bolivia lost its access to the Pacific Ocean after being defeated by which South American country?","correct":"Chile","wrong":["Peru","Brazil","Argentina"]},{"id":"9dac395649ed","q":"The assassination of which royal led to the start of World War I?","correct":"Archduke Franz Ferdinand","wrong":["Louis Mountbatten","King Charles I","Nicholas II"]},{"id":"8b847fb87f6c","q":"What was the name of the planned invasion of Japan towards the end of World War II?","correct":"Operation Downfall","wrong":["Operation Boarding Party","Operation Ironclad","Operation Aflame"]},{"id":"1c4dae59e530","q":"How many manned moon landings have there been?","correct":"6","wrong":["1","3","7"]},{"id":"a8852366d29e","q":"List the following Iranic empires in chronological order:","correct":"Median, Achaemenid, Parthian, Sassanid","wrong":["Median, Achaemenid, Sassanid, Parthian","Achaemenid, Median, Parthian, Sassanid","Achaemenid, Median, Sassanid, Parthian"]},{"id":"424924b71d10","q":"These two countries held a commonwealth from the 16th to 18th century.","correct":"Poland and Lithuania","wrong":["Hutu and Rwanda","North Korea and South Korea","Bangladesh and Bhutan"]},{"id":"572307b3b726","q":"What was the real name of the Albanian national leader Skanderbeg?","correct":"Gjergj Kastrioti","wrong":["Diturak Zhulati","Iskander Bejko","Mirash Krasniki"]},{"id":"7521f9b4fac5","q":"Which dictator killed the most people?","correct":"Mao Zedong","wrong":["Joseph Stalin","Adolf Hitler","Kim Il Sung"]},{"id":"81bb9a527f26","q":"The ancient city of Chichén Itz&aacute; was built by which civilization?","correct":"Mayans","wrong":["Aztecs","Incas","Toltecs"]},{"id":"e2f1097a0e71","q":"During World War I, which nation's monarchs were blood related?","correct":"England, Germany, Russia","wrong":["France, Russia, Germany","Serbia, Russia, Croatia","Germany, Spain, Austria"]},{"id":"546d718ebcc5","q":"Spain was formed in 1469 with the marriage of Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II of what other Iberian kingdom?","correct":"Aragon","wrong":["Galicia","Le&oacute;n","Navarre"]},{"id":"ad74530805fa","q":"The term Luddite originally applied to disgruntled workers in which industry?","correct":"Textile","wrong":["Farming","Mining","Ceramics"]},{"id":"8c394874bc5c","q":"The fraudelent doctor John R. Brinkley acummulated great fame and wealth in the early 1900s offering what service?","correct":"Goat testicles transplant","wrong":["Pig blood transfusion","Cow liver transplant","Turkey breast implants"]},{"id":"0a0c15fb6f69","q":"What disease crippled President Franklin D. Roosevelt and led him to help the nation find a cure?","correct":"Polio","wrong":["Cancer","Meningitis","HIV"]},{"id":"b4505dff709d","q":"Who was the Prime Minister of Japan when Japan declared war on the US?","correct":"Hideki Tojo","wrong":["Michinomiya Hirohito","Isoroku Yamamoto","Fumimaro Konoe"]},{"id":"27ecda88e28a","q":"Which game was the Game of the Year in 2018?","correct":"God of War","wrong":["Detroit: Become Human","Red Dead Redemption 2","A Way Out"]},{"id":"b9661436b755","q":"Who crowned Charlemagne as Holy Roman Emperor on Christmas Day in 800?","correct":"Pope Leo III","wrong":["Pope Urban IV","Pope Stephen V","Pope Valentine"]},{"id":"4743af341232","q":"Who discovered Penicillin?","correct":"Alexander Flemming","wrong":["Marie Curie","Alfred Nobel","Louis Pasteur"]},{"id":"f335983d6cc1","q":"The Fallingwater House, located in Pennsylvania, was designed by which architect?","correct":"Frank Lloyd Wright","wrong":["Antoni Gaudi","Frank Gehry","Le Corbusier"]},{"id":"a4184659ee39","q":"When did L. L. Zamenhof first publish \"Unua Libro\", the first publication describing his international language Esperanto?","correct":"1887","wrong":["1897","1905","1915"]},{"id":"9e5c7ebfefdd","q":"When did the United States formally declare war on Japan, entering World War II?","correct":"December 8, 1941","wrong":["June 6, 1944","June 22, 1941","September 1, 1939"]},{"id":"fe8e755b8c98","q":"The Little Entente was an alliance formed against which nation?","correct":"Hungary","wrong":["Germany","France","Prussia"]},{"id":"109372d8c110","q":"According to scholarly estimates, what percentage of the world population at the time died due to Tamerlane's conquests?","correct":"5%","wrong":["1%","3%","<1%"]},{"id":"9e23bb25e98b","q":"Who was the first American in space?","correct":"Alan Shephard","wrong":["Neil Armstrong","John Glenn","Jim Lovell"]},{"id":"20cf7442be8f","q":"Which Irish village in County Mayo built a tourism industry on the back of an alleged appearance by the Virgin Mary in 1879?","correct":"Knock","wrong":["Ballycastle","Swinford","Turlough"]},{"id":"381a77d9f33e","q":"America's Strategic Defense System during the Cold War was nicknamed after this famous movie.","correct":"Star Wars","wrong":["Jaws","Blade Runner","Alien"]},{"id":"ab0ce001c3e6","q":"Who was the first president of Kenya?","correct":"Jomo Kenyatta","wrong":["Daniel Moi","Tom Mboya","Oginga Odinga"]},{"id":"24de97063aac","q":"Which modern day country is the region that was known as Phrygia in ancient times?","correct":"Turkey","wrong":["Syria","Greece","Egypt"]},{"id":"47993f18d99c","q":"In what year did Kentucky become the 15th state to join the union?","correct":"1792","wrong":["1782","1798","1788"]},{"id":"0fe29aefc68a","q":"What happened on June 6, 1944?","correct":"D-Day","wrong":["Atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki","Attack on Pearl Harbor","The Liberation of Paris"]},{"id":"26d376449f2a","q":"When did Norway get its constitution?","correct":"1814","wrong":["1932","1905","1854"]},{"id":"9ea627bce0b3","q":"Where was Portuguese explorer Ferdinand Magellan killed in 1521?","correct":"The Phillipines","wrong":["Canary Islands","Guam","Argentina"]},{"id":"227127048e7c","q":"How many sonatas did Ludwig van Beethoven write?","correct":"32","wrong":["50","31","21"]},{"id":"65da0ea7eebc","q":"In addition to his career as an astrologer and \"prophet\", Nostradamus published a 1555 treatise that included a section on what?","correct":"Making jams and jellies","wrong":["Teaching parrots to talk","Cheating at card games","Digging graves"]},{"id":"a07d7dd69743","q":"What was the unofficial name for Germany between 1919 and 1933?","correct":"Weimar Republic","wrong":["German Democratic Republic","Federal Republic of Germany","Oesterreich"]},{"id":"a09da1850814","q":"The Spitfire L.F. Mk IX had what engine?","correct":"Merlin 66","wrong":["Griffon 65","Merlin 50","Merlin X"]},{"id":"3257b94315ff","q":"In what year was the last natural case of smallpox documented?","correct":"1977","wrong":["1982","1980","1990"]},{"id":"270b1e0c4f1e","q":"In 1845, a series of wars named after which indigenous people began in New Zealand?","correct":"Māori","wrong":["Papuans","Aborigines","Polynesians"]},{"id":"96c25791d88f","q":"How long did the Warsaw Uprising during World War II last?","correct":"63 Days","wrong":["20 Days","55 Days","224 Days"]},{"id":"35c2f5f28496","q":"Which building was set aflame on August 24th, 1812?","correct":"The White House","wrong":["Parliament Building","Grand National Assembly Building","Palace of the Nation"]},{"id":"864bc2717c18","q":"Which of the following years is commonly referred to as the \"Year Without a Summer\"?","correct":"1816","wrong":["1823","1813","1808"]},{"id":"d125c7ac8ecf","q":"How old was the famous King Tutankhamen (Tut) when he died?","correct":"19","wrong":["21","15","30"]},{"id":"58c424f37efb","q":"Who was Hannibal?","correct":"Carthaginian general","wrong":["British serial killer","French explorer","Greek philosopher"]},{"id":"366f08731578","q":"When did Spanish Peninsular War start?","correct":"1808","wrong":["1806","1810","1809"]},{"id":"4f23bec8d39f","q":"In what year did the First World War end?","correct":"1918","wrong":["1914","1916","1912"]},{"id":"f603187e065c","q":"In what year was the famous 45 foot tall Hollywood sign first erected?","correct":"1923","wrong":["1903","1913","1933"]},{"id":"3d1a76ea7a93","q":"How many women joined the United States Armed Services during World War II?","correct":"350,000","wrong":["225,000","100,000","500,000"]},{"id":"d681505889ca","q":"In which war did the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki occur?","correct":"World War II","wrong":["World War I","Russo-Japanese War","First Sino-Japanese War"]},{"id":"6cc52ae447b9","q":"With which Greek philosopher would you associate the phrase, \"I know that I know nothing\"?","correct":"Socrates","wrong":["Aristotle","Plato","Pythagoras"]},{"id":"3bbe1c3efd0e","q":"In the year 1900, what were the most popular first names given to boy and girl babies born in the United States?","correct":"John and Mary","wrong":["Joseph and Catherine","William and Elizabeth","George and Anne"]},{"id":"ac0f016c33fc","q":"Pol Pot was the former dictator of which country?","correct":"Cambodia","wrong":["Laos","North Korea","Vietnam"]},{"id":"dd39029e3cd0","q":"What was the name of the national hero of the Philippines who inspired and lead the Philippine Revolution against colonial Spain?","correct":"José Rizal","wrong":["Sim&oacute;n Bol&iacute;var","Benito Ju&aacute;rez","José de San Mart&iacute;n"]},{"id":"6867106ac5fa","q":"In what year did Texas secede from Mexico?","correct":"1836","wrong":["1838","1845","1844"]},{"id":"d5c08827de4c","q":"When did the Byzantine Empire collapse?","correct":"1453","wrong":["1299","1353","1498"]},{"id":"1486ac2efb3e","q":"To what political party did Abraham Lincoln belong when elected POTUS?","correct":"Republican","wrong":["Democrat","Independent","Whig"]},{"id":"58e31057996e","q":"Which one of these was not a beach landing site in the Invasion of Normandy?","correct":"Silver","wrong":["Gold","Juno","Sword"]},{"id":"a1b5385d0a60","q":"Which of the following is not in the Indo-European language family?","correct":"Finnish","wrong":["English","Hindi","Russian"]},{"id":"9e4588360e8c","q":"The minigun was designed in 1960 by which manufacturer.","correct":"General Electric","wrong":["Colt Firearms","Heckler & Koch","Sig Sauer"]},{"id":"950b36f18e01","q":"On which day did ARPANET suffer a 4 hour long network crash?","correct":"October 27, 1980","wrong":["November 21, 1969","October 29, 1969","December 9, 1991"]},{"id":"e68dfaa596a0","q":"Who was the first ruler of Haiti after the country had gained its independence?","correct":"Jean-Jacques Dessalines","wrong":["Toussaint Louverture","Henri Christophe","Alexandre Petion"]},{"id":"60b68829755d","q":"From 1940 to 1942, what was the capital-in-exile of Free France ?","correct":"Brazzaville","wrong":["Algiers","Paris","Tunis"]},{"id":"91b97daaec11","q":"What year was the Italian firearms manufacturer Beretta founded?","correct":"1526","wrong":["1776","1923","1998"]},{"id":"065c0255d754","q":"Which of the following countries was not an axis power during World War II?","correct":"Soviet Union","wrong":["Italy","Germany","Japan"]},{"id":"fdb11b91448d","q":"Who was the Confederate general in the American Civil War?","correct":"Robert E. Lee","wrong":["George A. Custer","Ulysses S. Grant","George B. McClellan"]},{"id":"a964c1cfc925","q":"In which year was Constantinople conquered by the Turks?","correct":"1453","wrong":["1435","1454","1440"]},{"id":"8e33c07374c9","q":"Who was the first president of the United States?","correct":"George Washington","wrong":["James Madison","Thomas Jefferson","James K. Polk"]},{"id":"191d945ec42e","q":"Which king was killed at the Battle of Bosworth Field in 1485?","correct":"Richard III","wrong":["Edward V","Henry VII","James I"]},{"id":"d11b280e97e4","q":"The RMS Titanic sunk during her maiden voyage from Southampton, England to which American city?","correct":"New York City","wrong":["Boston","Philadelphia","Washington"]},{"id":"753e1617ebee","q":"What year was the United States Declaration of Independence signed?","correct":"1776","wrong":["1775","1774","1777"]},{"id":"6f18d8dc6a7a","q":"Which Nation did NOT have a Colony in modern-day North America?","correct":"Portugal","wrong":["Spain","Sweden","Netherlands"]},{"id":"d39393536ef2","q":"Adolf Hitler was born on which date?","correct":"April 20, 1889","wrong":["June 12, 1889","February 6, 1889","April 16, 1889"]},{"id":"064e9092ff0d","q":"Which countries participated in the Lobster War?","correct":"France and Brazil","wrong":["Canada and Norway","Australia and New Zealand","United States and England"]},{"id":"340cbeb58056","q":"In 1547 who became the 1st Tsar of Russia","correct":"Ivan the Terrible","wrong":["Alexis of Russia","Mikhail Romanov","Peter the Great"]},{"id":"8d02452c8494","q":"What does the United States of America celebrate during the 4th of July?","correct":"The signing of the Declaration of Independence","wrong":["The anniversary of the Battle of Gettysburg","The crossing of the Delaware River","The ratification of the Constitution"]},{"id":"ed03f2fa835b","q":"Bohdan Khmelnytsky was which of the following?","correct":"Leader of the Ukrainian Cossacks","wrong":["General Secretary of the Communist Party of the USSR","Prince of Wallachia","Grand Prince of Novgorod"]},{"id":"666eb26d8d99","q":"Which of the following was Brazil was a former colony under?","correct":"Portugal","wrong":["Spain","The Netherlands","France"]},{"id":"de4a5b46be14","q":"Who was the President of the United States during the signing of the Gadsden Purchase?","correct":"Franklin Pierce","wrong":["Andrew Johnson","Abraham Lincoln","James Polk"]},{"id":"dfaa821c00ba","q":"Who was among those killed in the 2010 Smolensk, Russia plane crash tragedy?","correct":"The Polish President","wrong":["Pope John Paul II","Bang-Ding Ow","Albert Putin"]},{"id":"310fa88fb460","q":"The gunpowder plot was a well-known failed assassination attempt against which of England's then reigning monarchs?","correct":"James I","wrong":["Elizabeth I","Charles II","Charles I"]},{"id":"1e4745d7b1f2","q":"Who is attributed credit for recording the epic poem The Odyssey?","correct":"Homer","wrong":["Aristotle","Odysseus","Socrates"]},{"id":"8c9711fccd1a","q":"Which of the following battles is often considered as marking the beginning of the fall of the Western Roman Empire?","correct":"Battle of Adrianople","wrong":["Battle of Thessalonica","Battle of Pollentia","Battle of Constantinople"]},{"id":"d79ffdf90710","q":"Who was the first Chancellor of a united Germany in 1871?","correct":"Otto Von Bismark","wrong":["Kaiser Wilhelm","Fredrick the 2nd","Robert Koch"]},{"id":"b1bb92ad5cce","q":"Which British monarch was also known as \"William of Orange\"?","correct":"William III","wrong":["William I","William II","William IV"]},{"id":"adcfdd13f6b0","q":"What year did the Titanic sink?","correct":"1912","wrong":["1930","1917","1941"]},{"id":"91e769b8bde6","q":"On what day did Germany invade Poland?","correct":"September 1, 1939","wrong":["December 7, 1941","June 22, 1941","July 7, 1937"]},{"id":"81e00f306d42","q":"In what year did the Great Northern War, between Russia and Sweden, end?","correct":"1721","wrong":["1726","1727","1724"]}],"football":[{"id":"f90435ddabc3","q":"What nationality is John Willie Parker?","correct":"United Kingdom","wrong":["Tunisia","Samoa","United States"],"league":"pl"}